1
00:00:15,372 --> 00:00:16,372
(As of this moment,)

2
00:00:16,372 --> 00:00:18,942
(you can share everything about yourselves.)

3
00:00:19,472 --> 00:00:22,042
(Their age and job are finally revealed.)

4
00:00:22,612 --> 00:00:24,912
(As unexpected twists unfold,)

5
00:00:25,282 --> 00:00:28,722
(the residents' decisions take a turn.)

6
00:00:28,952 --> 00:00:31,022
(Just how interested is she in me?)

7
00:00:31,352 --> 00:00:33,892
(Kim Seon Ho does not have a date tomorrow.)

8
00:00:34,192 --> 00:00:35,192
(Are you going out on a date?)

9
00:00:35,192 --> 00:00:36,362
(No comment.)

10
00:00:36,692 --> 00:00:39,162
(A split-second decision creates a rift between them.)

11
00:00:40,062 --> 00:00:41,802
(I've been wanting to talk to you.)

12
00:00:42,202 --> 00:00:44,332
(Unexpressed feelings toward Seon Ho reach him.)

13
00:00:44,502 --> 00:00:47,542
(Honestly, I kept thinking about Seon Ho.)

14
00:00:48,272 --> 00:00:51,272
(Where do they stand amid the missed connections?)

15
00:00:52,012 --> 00:00:56,282
(Love Against Time)

16
00:00:56,812 --> 00:00:59,282
You can drop the honorifics, Seon Ho.

17
00:00:59,282 --> 00:01:00,582
Sure.

18
00:01:01,182 --> 00:01:04,092
You said the other day that you had a sore throat.

19
00:01:04,092 --> 00:01:05,592
I brought warm water just in case.

20
00:01:05,592 --> 00:01:07,122
- Really?
- Yes. Let me know if you need it.

21
00:01:07,122 --> 00:01:08,662
- You said it was pretty bad.
- What?

22
00:01:09,822 --> 00:01:12,462
- Seriously? You're so thoughtful.
- what?

23
00:01:14,632 --> 00:01:16,502
Na Young told me earlier that...

24
00:01:16,502 --> 00:01:18,372
it sounded like my voice was breaking.

25
00:01:18,372 --> 00:01:19,732
No. You sound the same.

26
00:01:19,732 --> 00:01:20,802
- Really? Actually, - Yes.

27
00:01:20,802 --> 00:01:23,102
my voice usually sounds prettier and more pleasant than this.

28
00:01:23,542 --> 00:01:24,872
(Smiling)

29
00:01:27,412 --> 00:01:29,282
- Isn't the weather great?
- It is.

30
00:01:29,282 --> 00:01:30,882
(Going out for the first time with someone she was interested in)

31
00:01:31,752 --> 00:01:35,322
We never engaged in a conversation in the House.

32
00:01:36,052 --> 00:01:39,322
I already had my 1st and 2nd choices in mind.

33
00:01:39,322 --> 00:01:42,262
I always wanted to talk to you because you were my second choice.

34
00:01:42,262 --> 00:01:43,292
Really?

35
00:01:45,532 --> 00:01:47,802
But did you want to talk to me?

36
00:01:47,802 --> 00:01:48,862
- Yes.
- Really?

37
00:01:48,862 --> 00:01:51,132
You were also the second person I was curious about.

38
00:01:51,132 --> 00:01:52,272
- Really?
- Yes.

39
00:01:52,632 --> 00:01:55,572
- Take the water out and drink it.
- I had no idea.

40
00:01:56,372 --> 00:01:58,142
- Oh, this? Is this it?
- Yes.

41
00:01:58,142 --> 00:01:59,372
- Yes.
- Why is it so big?

42
00:01:59,372 --> 00:02:01,642
- There's a lid here.
- I see. There's a lid.

43
00:02:02,112 --> 00:02:05,052
I looked for an insulated bottle. And that was the only one.

44
00:02:05,552 --> 00:02:07,522
- The temperature is perfect.
- Is it perfect?

45
00:02:07,522 --> 00:02:08,652
Gosh, this is nice.

46
00:02:08,952 --> 00:02:10,022
That's good.

47
00:02:14,162 --> 00:02:15,392
I didn't know.

48
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:20,962
I wanted to talk to you, so I said things like...

49
00:02:20,962 --> 00:02:24,072
"Where are you going, Seon Ho?" I asked you that several times.

50
00:02:24,972 --> 00:02:26,232
- Yes, you did.
- Right? I did.

51
00:02:26,232 --> 00:02:27,672
And I just did a little bow.

52
00:02:27,672 --> 00:02:29,172
I said things like, "There." And I left.

53
00:02:29,802 --> 00:02:32,612
- But it didn't show...
- Yes?

54
00:02:34,212 --> 00:02:35,542
at all.

55
00:02:38,982 --> 00:02:42,622
The thing is, I only smile at the people I'm interested in.

56
00:02:42,622 --> 00:02:45,852
But you smile at everyone.

57
00:02:46,592 --> 00:02:48,262
So I couldn't tell.

58
00:02:49,462 --> 00:02:52,362
When I'm flustered, I can't help but smile.

59
00:02:52,362 --> 00:02:55,032
- Really?
- Especially when I'm nervous.

60
00:02:55,532 --> 00:02:58,132
You have the prettiest smile. Did you know that?

61
00:02:58,632 --> 00:03:00,202
You have the most beautiful smile.

62
00:03:01,042 --> 00:03:03,142
Really? Thank you. Gosh.

63
00:03:03,402 --> 00:03:05,412
- My goodness.
- Oh, my.

64
00:03:05,412 --> 00:03:06,612
(Lee Se Young)

65
00:03:06,612 --> 00:03:08,082
- I'm curious about these two.
- Yes, me too.

66
00:03:08,082 --> 00:03:09,582
I actually think they might hit it off.

67
00:03:09,582 --> 00:03:11,982
This is a good chance for Seon Ho to get to know Ro Bin.

68
00:03:11,982 --> 00:03:14,152
- He can get to know her better now.
- Yes. He can totally do that.

69
00:03:14,152 --> 00:03:15,982
- I agree.
- A party for the unchosen ones.

70
00:03:16,322 --> 00:03:17,322
(The party for the unchosen ones takes place in the House.)

71
00:03:17,322 --> 00:03:19,452
- I bet they're happy this happened.
- This actually worked out for them.

72
00:03:19,452 --> 00:03:21,192
- It ended up helping them instead.
- Yes.

73
00:03:21,192 --> 00:03:23,322
That's why this is making me nervous.

74
00:03:23,392 --> 00:03:24,892
I think they're going to hit it off.

75
00:03:24,892 --> 00:03:26,032
- You think they'll hit it off?
- Is that so, Ye Ji?

76
00:03:26,032 --> 00:03:27,862
- I'm worried about Ye Ji.
- You think so, Ye Ji?

77
00:03:28,002 --> 00:03:29,062
Wait, she's not Ye Ji.

78
00:03:29,062 --> 00:03:30,872
- Wait. What was that about?
- I'm sorry.

79
00:03:30,902 --> 00:03:32,402
(Ye Na is feeling for Ye Ji every week.)

80
00:03:32,532 --> 00:03:34,072
You know, Ye Ji...

81
00:03:34,842 --> 00:03:36,802
chose Do Gon out of spite...

82
00:03:36,802 --> 00:03:37,972
in the heat of the moment.

83
00:03:37,972 --> 00:03:39,172
- Right.
- Then they got to go on a date.

84
00:03:39,442 --> 00:03:41,212
- But...
- So they went on a date.

85
00:03:41,212 --> 00:03:43,342
While she was on a date with Do Gon,

86
00:03:43,642 --> 00:03:44,952
her head was filled with thoughts...

87
00:03:44,952 --> 00:03:46,282
- about Seon Ho.
- She only thought about him.

88
00:03:46,282 --> 00:03:48,352
- She felt bad for him.
- She felt bad.

89
00:03:48,352 --> 00:03:50,352
- Right.
- This is driving me crazy.

90
00:03:50,992 --> 00:03:53,252
Then did you get a chance to talk to everyone?

91
00:03:53,252 --> 00:03:54,662
No. I...

92
00:03:54,662 --> 00:03:55,662
With only one person?

93
00:03:55,662 --> 00:03:59,392
I've only talked to one lady I went on a date with.

94
00:03:59,392 --> 00:04:00,692
- Really?
- Yes.

95
00:04:01,032 --> 00:04:02,302
- Yes.
- I see.

96
00:04:02,402 --> 00:04:06,202
Are you an expressive type when you're in a relationship?

97
00:04:06,202 --> 00:04:07,272
Yes, when I'm in a relationship.

98
00:04:07,272 --> 00:04:08,302
- You're expressive?
- Totally.

99
00:04:08,302 --> 00:04:11,072
I don't have to hide my feelings when I'm in a relationship.

100
00:04:12,112 --> 00:04:15,442
(They're sharing a conversation for the first time.)

101
00:04:15,712 --> 00:04:16,982
You're a great driver.

102
00:04:16,982 --> 00:04:19,752
(The two of them arrive near the bakery.)

103
00:04:20,312 --> 00:04:22,982
Do you know where the cafe is? I mean, the bakery?

104
00:04:23,322 --> 00:04:25,592
- Wait. It's...
- Okay.

105
00:04:25,892 --> 00:04:26,892
Wait.

106
00:04:28,862 --> 00:04:30,362
(Looking around)

107
00:04:32,162 --> 00:04:33,492
Hold on, Seon Ho.

108
00:04:35,132 --> 00:04:36,402
I can't see.

109
00:04:37,232 --> 00:04:38,702
Hold on a second.

110
00:04:38,872 --> 00:04:39,972
Thank you.

111
00:04:39,972 --> 00:04:41,172
(Covering)

112
00:04:41,172 --> 00:04:42,372
What's this?

113
00:04:42,942 --> 00:04:44,272
(Heart-pounding)

114
00:04:44,272 --> 00:04:45,672
Gosh, hold on.

115
00:04:45,672 --> 00:04:47,112
He's covering her head.

116
00:04:47,112 --> 00:04:48,412
- This.
- Yes.

117
00:04:48,412 --> 00:04:49,742
You know what?

118
00:04:49,742 --> 00:04:52,852
I think we're all very much charmed by Seon Ho.

119
00:04:52,852 --> 00:04:54,522
We usually let these gestures go without making a comment.

120
00:04:54,522 --> 00:04:55,522
- Right.
- But we're pointing out...

121
00:04:55,522 --> 00:04:56,522
everything he does.

122
00:04:56,522 --> 00:04:57,722
- It's like when he's breathing, - Everything he does.

123
00:04:57,722 --> 00:04:59,022
we'd be like, "Why are you breathing like that?"

124
00:04:59,352 --> 00:05:00,392
(Obsessing over Seon Ho's action)

125
00:05:00,392 --> 00:05:02,822
- "Why drink water like that?" - We're giving it meaning.

126
00:05:02,822 --> 00:05:04,692
- We're doing that to everything.
- Yes.

127
00:05:04,692 --> 00:05:06,732
- I think we should calm down first.
- Right.

128
00:05:06,732 --> 00:05:07,862
- That's right.
- Right?

129
00:05:07,862 --> 00:05:08,862
- I'm sorry.
- We should calm down.

130
00:05:08,862 --> 00:05:10,502
- Let's stop doing that.
- We forgot to do our job.

131
00:05:11,302 --> 00:05:13,732
(Pondering)

132
00:05:13,902 --> 00:05:15,342
Why are they standing so close?

133
00:05:16,842 --> 00:05:18,372
- Why is he so tall?
- Why is he so tall?

134
00:05:18,372 --> 00:05:19,642
Why does he look taller today?

135
00:05:19,772 --> 00:05:20,942
Why is he covering her so well?

136
00:05:22,012 --> 00:05:24,012
(We're watching.)

137
00:05:24,512 --> 00:05:25,712
What's this?

138
00:05:27,012 --> 00:05:29,022
I see. This is the bakery.

139
00:05:30,082 --> 00:05:31,152
- Is that the one?
- Yes.

140
00:05:31,152 --> 00:05:32,492
I don't think it is.

141
00:05:32,492 --> 00:05:33,492
That's not it.

142
00:05:33,752 --> 00:05:34,962
Wait, Seon Ho.

143
00:05:35,992 --> 00:05:37,492
Where are we now?

144
00:05:37,492 --> 00:05:38,662
(Getting close)

145
00:05:40,132 --> 00:05:41,432
Let's go this way.

146
00:05:42,802 --> 00:05:44,032
Let's go this way.

147
00:05:44,032 --> 00:05:45,632
We have to take the long way around.

148
00:05:46,532 --> 00:05:47,572
Okay.

149
00:05:47,572 --> 00:05:49,342
(Seon Ho locates the bakery.)

150
00:05:50,902 --> 00:05:52,212
- Is this the place?
- Yes.

151
00:05:54,912 --> 00:05:57,512
Do you want to buy the bread and head back right away?

152
00:05:57,512 --> 00:05:58,682
That sounds good too.

153
00:05:58,682 --> 00:06:01,522
Let's do that then. We can just buy some bread.

154
00:06:03,152 --> 00:06:04,152
Do you like bread?

155
00:06:04,152 --> 00:06:05,152
- Me?
- Yes.

156
00:06:05,152 --> 00:06:06,592
I enjoy eating it when it's available.

157
00:06:06,592 --> 00:06:07,662
You do?

158
00:06:07,662 --> 00:06:09,862
- Then...
- What kind of bread do you like?

159
00:06:09,862 --> 00:06:12,262
I'm not picky. I like everything.

160
00:06:13,062 --> 00:06:15,232
First, let's get some morning rolls.

161
00:06:15,232 --> 00:06:16,262
- Okay.
- And...

162
00:06:16,432 --> 00:06:17,872
- let's get one of these.
- This looks good.

163
00:06:17,872 --> 00:06:18,872
- Right?
- Yes.

164
00:06:19,932 --> 00:06:21,372
- Olives? This looks good.
- Yes.

165
00:06:21,902 --> 00:06:23,302
- What's this?
- What's this?

166
00:06:23,872 --> 00:06:26,012
- Do you want to try this?
- Yes.

167
00:06:26,372 --> 00:06:27,712
- Great.
- This should be enough.

168
00:06:27,712 --> 00:06:29,082
- That...
- I'll carry that.

169
00:06:29,282 --> 00:06:30,412
What's this?

170
00:06:31,752 --> 00:06:34,012
- This looks good too.
- Let's get that too.

171
00:06:35,522 --> 00:06:36,722
This too.

172
00:06:36,722 --> 00:06:38,652
Are we buying too much?

173
00:06:39,692 --> 00:06:41,492
Is this enough? There are eight of us.

174
00:06:41,492 --> 00:06:42,922
- This should be more than enough.
- You think so?

175
00:06:42,922 --> 00:06:44,332
Some people might not eat it.

176
00:06:44,332 --> 00:06:45,632
- Guessing their portion is hard.
- Right.

177
00:06:47,492 --> 00:06:48,562
Thank you.

178
00:06:49,332 --> 00:06:51,102
- Thank you. Bye.
- Bye.

179
00:06:51,102 --> 00:06:52,772
(How will their day in the House go?)

180
00:06:52,772 --> 00:06:54,872
- This is going to taste so good.
- It's a lot of food.

181
00:06:56,742 --> 00:07:00,172
(Meanwhile, Ryun Gi and Min Young are going on a date.)

182
00:07:01,312 --> 00:07:02,442
- I...
- Are you feeling okay?

183
00:07:02,442 --> 00:07:03,442
- Am I feeling okay?
- Yes.

184
00:07:03,442 --> 00:07:05,252
I'm full of energy right now...

185
00:07:05,252 --> 00:07:07,682
- Really? Then...
- because the meds...

186
00:07:07,922 --> 00:07:10,282
- have worn off a lot.
- Really?

187
00:07:10,582 --> 00:07:12,522
- Right. You were on chemo. Right?
- Yes.

188
00:07:12,522 --> 00:07:15,192
The chemo side effects are pretty rough.

189
00:07:15,192 --> 00:07:16,222
Right.

190
00:07:16,222 --> 00:07:18,092
How many more rounds do you have left?

191
00:07:18,092 --> 00:07:20,062
I have to get eight rounds.

192
00:07:20,062 --> 00:07:22,002
- I'm on the fourth one now.
- That's good.

193
00:07:22,002 --> 00:07:23,502
- I'm halfway there.
- Yes.

194
00:07:24,372 --> 00:07:27,432
What's important is that I keep losing weight.

195
00:07:27,432 --> 00:07:30,942
It feels like my energy is weakening.

196
00:07:31,002 --> 00:07:32,842
- That's the hard part.
- You know what?

197
00:07:33,142 --> 00:07:36,882
I also lost about 27kg or 28kg.

198
00:07:37,342 --> 00:07:38,652
I didn't realize it back then.

199
00:07:38,652 --> 00:07:40,212
But my legs were so bony like chopsticks.

200
00:07:40,312 --> 00:07:42,282
I lost weight to the point of looking sick.

201
00:07:42,282 --> 00:07:43,322
Right.

202
00:07:43,582 --> 00:07:45,522
But I gained the weight back once it was over.

203
00:07:45,622 --> 00:07:47,552
So it will come back.

204
00:07:48,292 --> 00:07:49,462
- Thank you...
- Sure.

205
00:07:49,462 --> 00:07:50,692
for saying that.

206
00:07:50,922 --> 00:07:52,462
I don't know yet.

207
00:07:55,202 --> 00:07:57,302
That's why when people get sick,

208
00:07:57,302 --> 00:07:59,632
they talk less and act more carefully...

209
00:07:59,632 --> 00:08:00,832
around other people.

210
00:08:00,832 --> 00:08:02,842
I think because of that, people can't see your charms.

211
00:08:03,042 --> 00:08:04,302
You can date anyone you want...

212
00:08:04,302 --> 00:08:05,442
if you can be yourself like this.

213
00:08:05,812 --> 00:08:07,672
- I can date anyone I want?
- Yes. I mean it.

214
00:08:09,582 --> 00:08:11,582
This is when your self-esteem is low.

215
00:08:11,582 --> 00:08:13,852
- Right.
- When she doesn't like you back,

216
00:08:13,882 --> 00:08:15,922
you'd think, "I knew it. It's because I'm sick."

217
00:08:15,922 --> 00:08:18,152
"I'm not enough for her." You start blaming yourself.

218
00:08:18,152 --> 00:08:19,192
- Right.
- But...

219
00:08:19,622 --> 00:08:22,322
looking back, you have to think like you're a prince.

220
00:08:22,422 --> 00:08:23,922
When she doesn't like you back,

221
00:08:23,922 --> 00:08:25,662
- you should go, "Oh, no." - What?

222
00:08:26,462 --> 00:08:28,402
"She doesn't like me."

223
00:08:28,402 --> 00:08:30,602
- "It's her loss." - "How dare she..."

224
00:08:30,602 --> 00:08:31,832
- "not like me back?" - Right.

225
00:08:31,832 --> 00:08:33,472
"Poor thing. It's her loss."

226
00:08:33,472 --> 00:08:34,642
That's what you should think.

227
00:08:35,202 --> 00:08:37,102
So don't put too much pressure on yourself.

228
00:08:37,572 --> 00:08:38,942
Just go for it.

229
00:08:40,412 --> 00:08:41,682
Having a friend like Min Young...

230
00:08:41,682 --> 00:08:43,142
- would be so reliable.
- Exactly.

231
00:08:43,142 --> 00:08:44,242
She'd boost your self-esteem.

232
00:08:44,242 --> 00:08:46,882
It's not just a regular date. Looking at how it's going,

233
00:08:46,952 --> 00:08:48,622
they're talking about their illness...

234
00:08:48,622 --> 00:08:49,622
and she's trying to boost his self-esteem.

235
00:08:49,622 --> 00:08:50,622
- This is nice.
- Right.

236
00:08:51,352 --> 00:08:52,922
- It's a helpful date too.
- I agree.

237
00:08:53,552 --> 00:08:54,762
That's why...

238
00:08:55,322 --> 00:08:57,122
when we were preparing dinner last night,

239
00:08:58,132 --> 00:09:00,062
I decided to keep an open mind...

240
00:09:00,062 --> 00:09:02,602
and try to talk to more people.

241
00:09:02,602 --> 00:09:03,762
- Right.
- That's what I thought.

242
00:09:04,332 --> 00:09:05,772
Yesterday was just the beginning for me.

243
00:09:05,772 --> 00:09:06,902
- Everything is...
- That's good.

244
00:09:07,232 --> 00:09:08,302
starting now.

245
00:09:08,302 --> 00:09:09,402
You're amazing.

246
00:09:13,612 --> 00:09:18,382
(They arrive at the first spot.)

247
00:09:18,382 --> 00:09:20,012
- Let's park it here.
- Yes.

248
00:09:20,582 --> 00:09:22,152
We're going to the Han River today.

249
00:09:22,382 --> 00:09:23,552
Really? No way.

250
00:09:23,552 --> 00:09:24,622
- The weather is amazing.
- Yes.

251
00:09:24,622 --> 00:09:25,822
We're going to the Han River.

252
00:09:26,052 --> 00:09:29,822
We're going to pick up the picnic set here.

253
00:09:29,992 --> 00:09:31,232
You're so thoughtful.

254
00:09:32,232 --> 00:09:35,162
(Thoughtful Ryun Gi planned a Han River date.)

255
00:09:35,162 --> 00:09:36,162
- Is this the place?
- Yes.

256
00:09:36,162 --> 00:09:38,202
- What a cute puppy. Hello.
- Hi.

257
00:09:40,102 --> 00:09:41,102
Hi.

258
00:09:41,542 --> 00:09:43,702
- You're not afraid of dogs.
- I have a dog.

259
00:09:43,842 --> 00:09:44,842
What?

260
00:09:46,742 --> 00:09:48,982
- They're super friendly.
- My goodness.

261
00:09:49,542 --> 00:09:50,612
(Min Young, the dog owner, pats the dog like a pro.)

262
00:09:50,612 --> 00:09:52,382
Aren't you a cute puppy?

263
00:09:53,382 --> 00:09:54,552
Min Young, you can pick the toast.

264
00:09:54,552 --> 00:09:56,022
- I'll pick the sandwich.
- Yes.

265
00:09:57,082 --> 00:09:59,692
- Kaya ham cheese toast.
- Kaya ham cheese toast.

266
00:10:00,122 --> 00:10:02,222
- We'll take the bulgogi sandwich.
- Bulgogi sandwich.

267
00:10:03,122 --> 00:10:04,862
- That's all.
- Yes.

268
00:10:05,392 --> 00:10:08,032
No.

269
00:10:08,302 --> 00:10:11,972
(Min Young quickly pays for the food.)

270
00:10:13,032 --> 00:10:14,172
You get the next one.

271
00:10:15,902 --> 00:10:16,972
This isn't good.

272
00:10:19,072 --> 00:10:20,212
I can't let you pay.

273
00:10:20,512 --> 00:10:21,612
- I'm cool like that.
- Thank you.

274
00:10:21,612 --> 00:10:22,682
You...

275
00:10:23,642 --> 00:10:25,582
- I'll prepare the drinks too.
- Thank you.

276
00:10:25,912 --> 00:10:27,052
How beautiful.

277
00:10:28,082 --> 00:10:29,382
It's acting like a baby.

278
00:10:29,382 --> 00:10:31,552
Right. The dog suddenly came into my arms.

279
00:10:32,352 --> 00:10:35,692
It really looks like a baby. Like a human baby.

280
00:10:38,092 --> 00:10:40,162
I'm doing my own research now.

281
00:10:40,162 --> 00:10:41,192
What research?

282
00:10:41,192 --> 00:10:42,632
I want to know how I can make good use of...

283
00:10:42,632 --> 00:10:44,062
- this camera.
- Look.

284
00:10:45,632 --> 00:10:49,672
(He naturally takes pictures of Min Young.)

285
00:10:51,672 --> 00:10:52,772
That one came out nicely.

286
00:10:55,342 --> 00:10:58,782
(A cute girl with a cute puppy)

287
00:11:01,822 --> 00:11:03,482
It's cute because it's big.

288
00:11:04,282 --> 00:11:05,822
(Glancing over)

289
00:11:06,722 --> 00:11:08,092
When I first met you,

290
00:11:08,092 --> 00:11:10,462
I didn't expect this kind of vibe from you.

291
00:11:10,462 --> 00:11:11,792
- Me? Really?
- Yes.

292
00:11:11,792 --> 00:11:12,832
Why is that?

293
00:11:13,392 --> 00:11:17,302
When we first met, I noticed that you were very shy.

294
00:11:17,302 --> 00:11:18,302
Yes.

295
00:11:19,632 --> 00:11:22,672
I haven't been on a lot of dates with guys.

296
00:11:22,902 --> 00:11:23,972
- You haven't had many boyfriends?
- So...

297
00:11:23,972 --> 00:11:25,212
- I haven't had a lot of boyfriends.
- Okay.

298
00:11:25,412 --> 00:11:26,612
I don't like doing things with people...

299
00:11:26,612 --> 00:11:27,772
I don't feel comfortable around.

300
00:11:28,442 --> 00:11:29,612
And it shows.

301
00:11:29,612 --> 00:11:30,642
But...

302
00:11:31,952 --> 00:11:33,882
after talking to you quite a bit,

303
00:11:33,882 --> 00:11:35,182
I thought it'd be fun to go out with you.

304
00:11:35,282 --> 00:11:36,982
I wanted to talk to you a bit more too.

305
00:11:37,552 --> 00:11:38,752
- Thank you.
- So I chose you.

306
00:11:38,752 --> 00:11:39,952
Then we got to go on a date.

307
00:11:40,322 --> 00:11:41,362
Did it make you feel good?

308
00:11:41,362 --> 00:11:42,392
Yes. I was like, "Does he feel the same way?"

309
00:11:42,392 --> 00:11:43,422
That's good.

310
00:11:44,322 --> 00:11:45,992
(Gazing)

311
00:11:48,832 --> 00:11:49,932
Actually,

312
00:11:51,572 --> 00:11:52,772
- when...
- Yes?

313
00:11:54,002 --> 00:11:56,172
I was crying in the kitchen, you came over.

314
00:11:56,402 --> 00:11:58,112
- The things you told me...
- Yes?

315
00:11:58,372 --> 00:12:00,672
- made you sound very experienced.
- Really?

316
00:12:01,072 --> 00:12:03,112
(Day One)

317
00:12:03,382 --> 00:12:06,712
(Ryun Gi was crying alone after reading his journal.)

318
00:12:07,452 --> 00:12:08,452
What is it?

319
00:12:08,452 --> 00:12:09,452
(Min Young approached Ryun Gi.)

320
00:12:09,452 --> 00:12:10,982
- Who made you cry?
- No.

321
00:12:12,522 --> 00:12:13,622
Don't cry.

322
00:12:16,822 --> 00:12:18,432
Everyone is so amazing.

323
00:12:19,132 --> 00:12:20,262
You're amazing too.

324
00:12:22,002 --> 00:12:23,302
You should be proud of it.

325
00:12:23,532 --> 00:12:24,902
You can brag about it to people.

326
00:12:26,002 --> 00:12:27,002
I mean it.

327
00:12:27,002 --> 00:12:28,972
(Her kind words comforted him.)

328
00:12:31,342 --> 00:12:32,472
- Gosh.
- I see.

329
00:12:32,572 --> 00:12:34,272
I might fall in love with her.

330
00:12:34,272 --> 00:12:36,242
Me too. I would be so grateful.

331
00:12:36,242 --> 00:12:38,782
- Right.
- Exactly. I mean, he cried.

332
00:12:38,852 --> 00:12:40,882
- He showed her the real him.
- Yes.

333
00:12:40,882 --> 00:12:43,482
You rarely get to see this real side...

334
00:12:43,482 --> 00:12:45,392
- of anyone. You know?
- Right.

335
00:12:45,492 --> 00:12:47,122
- You rarely show it to people.
- Right.

336
00:12:47,122 --> 00:12:49,162
On top of that, she comforted him.

337
00:12:49,162 --> 00:12:51,362
If I were him, I would be impressed by her.

338
00:12:51,362 --> 00:12:52,832
- She embraced his pain.
- She did.

339
00:12:52,832 --> 00:12:55,002
- I'd fall in love then. Yes.
- He might rely on her too.

340
00:12:56,702 --> 00:13:00,302
You sounded nonchalant when you told me those things.

341
00:13:00,302 --> 00:13:01,402
But to me,

342
00:13:02,272 --> 00:13:03,442
you sounded experienced.

343
00:13:04,542 --> 00:13:07,042
- But... Really?
- And I was grateful for that.

344
00:13:07,142 --> 00:13:10,042
I wanted to tell you about how I felt if there was a time for it.

345
00:13:10,982 --> 00:13:14,282
Actually, I always ended up in a relationship...

346
00:13:15,052 --> 00:13:17,022
with someone comfortable...

347
00:13:17,022 --> 00:13:18,492
- like you.
- Really?

348
00:13:18,492 --> 00:13:20,722
I only dated people I've known for a long time.

349
00:13:20,722 --> 00:13:21,892
I see.

350
00:13:21,892 --> 00:13:23,522
There were times...

351
00:13:23,522 --> 00:13:25,792
when friendships turned into romantic relationships.

352
00:13:26,532 --> 00:13:28,162
Of course, other couples might get more butterflies...

353
00:13:28,162 --> 00:13:29,802
in the beginning of their relationship.

354
00:13:30,362 --> 00:13:31,672
I want someone...

355
00:13:31,672 --> 00:13:33,402
whom I can feel comfortable with even if we're not doing...

356
00:13:33,872 --> 00:13:35,002
anything special.

357
00:13:36,102 --> 00:13:37,772
You seemed comfortable in the House.

358
00:13:38,412 --> 00:13:40,972
So I wondered if you weren't interested in anyone.

359
00:13:40,972 --> 00:13:42,082
That crossed my mind.

360
00:13:43,512 --> 00:13:44,782
Should I be more serious then?

361
00:13:46,682 --> 00:13:47,712
(Smiling)

362
00:13:48,252 --> 00:13:50,522
(The two of them are growing closer...)

363
00:13:50,522 --> 00:13:52,822
(balancing between comfort and excitement.)

364
00:13:53,952 --> 00:13:55,522
Let's go.

365
00:13:57,262 --> 00:13:58,832
This is a therapeutic date.

366
00:14:01,362 --> 00:14:04,162
(Hangang Park)

367
00:14:05,072 --> 00:14:09,442
(A fresh spring breeze is blowing over Hangang Park.)

368
00:14:11,942 --> 00:14:14,142
- This place is beautiful.
- Yes.

369
00:14:15,942 --> 00:14:18,212
- The weather is great.
- Which way should we go?

370
00:14:18,512 --> 00:14:19,552
Over there.

371
00:14:20,552 --> 00:14:21,922
What a great spot.

372
00:14:24,952 --> 00:14:28,662
(Their Han River date is off to a great start.)

373
00:14:29,562 --> 00:14:31,062
Gosh, it's beautiful indeed.

374
00:14:31,962 --> 00:14:33,732
(The two of them set up in a breezy area.)

375
00:14:33,732 --> 00:14:35,302
It's so beautiful. Wait.

376
00:14:35,762 --> 00:14:37,262
(Staring)

377
00:14:41,942 --> 00:14:44,172
- Why? You look great today.
- What?

378
00:14:44,342 --> 00:14:45,572
I'm wearing a lot of makeup today.

379
00:14:47,072 --> 00:14:49,382
- Shall we?
- Thank you.

380
00:14:49,612 --> 00:14:50,842
Should I kneel down here?

381
00:14:51,142 --> 00:14:52,352
(Bursting into laughter)

382
00:14:53,452 --> 00:14:55,782
(Ryun Gi makes Min Young laugh.)

383
00:14:55,782 --> 00:14:57,082
You're so funny that you're making me drool.

384
00:14:57,222 --> 00:14:58,892
- How do you feel? Hungry yet?
- Yes.

385
00:14:59,152 --> 00:15:00,892
A dessert sounds perfect now.

386
00:15:00,892 --> 00:15:01,922
Nice.

387
00:15:02,192 --> 00:15:03,992
Actually, that's why...

388
00:15:04,522 --> 00:15:06,632
Once you see this, you're going to be so surprised.

389
00:15:06,632 --> 00:15:07,692
Show me.

390
00:15:07,992 --> 00:15:09,202
What is it? Show me.

391
00:15:12,802 --> 00:15:13,902
Like this?

392
00:15:14,532 --> 00:15:16,172
- Ta-da.
- That's great.

393
00:15:16,172 --> 00:15:17,642
You're so sweet.

394
00:15:17,642 --> 00:15:19,472
- What do you think? Is it touching?
- This is so touching. Yes.

395
00:15:20,042 --> 00:15:22,882
It's so touching. You brought my favorite dessert.

396
00:15:23,612 --> 00:15:25,782
Let's eat little by little. Take your time.

397
00:15:25,952 --> 00:15:26,952
Okay.

398
00:15:30,482 --> 00:15:32,652
(Munching on the snack)

399
00:15:32,792 --> 00:15:34,792
- You really like those crackers.
- Yes.

400
00:15:34,792 --> 00:15:36,022
I can't seem to forget that.

401
00:15:36,022 --> 00:15:37,062
Thank you so much.

402
00:15:40,932 --> 00:15:41,962
How beautiful.

403
00:15:42,902 --> 00:15:43,932
What a relaxing day.

404
00:15:43,932 --> 00:15:45,872
Yes. You can relax today.

405
00:15:47,102 --> 00:15:48,802
It was fun to find out everyone's age and job yesterday.

406
00:15:48,802 --> 00:15:50,242
Right. Seriously.

407
00:15:50,572 --> 00:15:51,942
Whose information shocked you the most?

408
00:15:52,472 --> 00:15:53,672
- You.
- Me?

409
00:15:53,672 --> 00:15:54,712
- Really?
- Yes.

410
00:15:54,942 --> 00:15:56,112
You were nothing like I imagined.

411
00:15:58,982 --> 00:16:01,452
I don't look like a researcher, right?

412
00:16:01,452 --> 00:16:02,452
No.

413
00:16:03,022 --> 00:16:04,682
I didn't know you were that smart.

414
00:16:06,292 --> 00:16:07,822
You're like one of those guys I'd see at church.

415
00:16:08,922 --> 00:16:09,962
It was an unexpected charm.

416
00:16:11,562 --> 00:16:13,792
You didn't know I was that smart?

417
00:16:14,292 --> 00:16:16,102
I don't know much about researchers.

418
00:16:16,102 --> 00:16:18,972
But I thought they had to be incredibly smart to be one.

419
00:16:19,932 --> 00:16:21,672
I was like, "He's that smart?"

420
00:16:22,142 --> 00:16:23,802
- Do you need an armored vehicle?
- Yes, totally.

421
00:16:23,802 --> 00:16:25,672
Tell me how you make one of those.

422
00:16:27,812 --> 00:16:29,682
(Finding her adorable)

423
00:16:32,112 --> 00:16:35,252
I think some dust got in my eye because of the breeze.

424
00:16:36,282 --> 00:16:37,482
Do you need to get rid of it? Do you need help?

425
00:16:37,952 --> 00:16:40,122
- I think I got it out.
- No, you didn't.

426
00:16:40,122 --> 00:16:41,592
(Getting closer)

427
00:16:42,222 --> 00:16:43,222
It's still in your eye.

428
00:16:43,222 --> 00:16:44,662
(Worried)

429
00:16:44,662 --> 00:16:45,862
My glitter.

430
00:16:46,292 --> 00:16:47,332
Don't look!

431
00:16:47,992 --> 00:16:49,002
Why are you looking at me?

432
00:16:49,262 --> 00:16:50,832
- I don't know.
- It's going in.

433
00:16:52,472 --> 00:16:53,902
- It didn't come out.
- Don't look.

434
00:16:53,972 --> 00:16:56,272
- It didn't come out.
- I know.

435
00:16:58,712 --> 00:17:01,512
- Seriously.
- This looks like a relationship...

436
00:17:01,512 --> 00:17:02,542
- between two comfortable friends.
- Right.

437
00:17:02,542 --> 00:17:03,782
They're so cute together.

438
00:17:03,782 --> 00:17:06,182
When girls tell you not to look, you shouldn't.

439
00:17:06,182 --> 00:17:07,852
- We really can't?
- You can't.

440
00:17:07,852 --> 00:17:09,222
- Really?
- We can't tease you more.

441
00:17:09,222 --> 00:17:10,322
- We really shouldn't look?
- You really shouldn't.

442
00:17:10,322 --> 00:17:11,322
We don't want you to look.

443
00:17:11,322 --> 00:17:12,652
- For real?
- Yes.

444
00:17:12,652 --> 00:17:14,722
At first, we'll be gentle and say, "Oh, don't look."

445
00:17:14,722 --> 00:17:15,922
But after a couple of times, we'd go,

446
00:17:15,922 --> 00:17:17,262
"I told you to stop."

447
00:17:18,962 --> 00:17:19,962
"Why are you doing that?"

448
00:17:19,962 --> 00:17:21,802
- Things will get awkward then.
- Yes.

449
00:17:21,802 --> 00:17:24,902
Then we won't say anything the whole day.

450
00:17:28,402 --> 00:17:29,702
Why? You don't like that?

451
00:17:35,342 --> 00:17:36,942
This is a fun date.

452
00:17:37,842 --> 00:17:39,012
You're so funny.

453
00:17:39,012 --> 00:17:40,652
I'm comfortable and having a lot of fun.

454
00:17:40,652 --> 00:17:41,652
- Really?
- Yes.

455
00:17:42,482 --> 00:17:43,852
- That's a good thing, right?
- It's great.

456
00:17:44,422 --> 00:17:46,292
You're probably the only one I feel this comfortable around.

457
00:17:46,292 --> 00:17:47,552
I feel like I've been chosen.

458
00:17:47,552 --> 00:17:49,162
Yes. That's exactly it.

459
00:17:50,392 --> 00:17:53,392
Min Young took the lead in making me feel comfortable.

460
00:17:53,492 --> 00:17:55,632
So the mood between us relaxed.

461
00:17:55,632 --> 00:17:57,862
And I could be myself around her.

462
00:17:58,332 --> 00:17:59,732
I could feel...

463
00:18:00,002 --> 00:18:03,202
different things when I spent time with her.

464
00:18:03,702 --> 00:18:07,172
So she kept surprising me.

465
00:18:08,312 --> 00:18:11,712
(How will they remember their date today?)

466
00:18:13,212 --> 00:18:14,682
What... Wait. The breeze...

467
00:18:14,782 --> 00:18:16,252
It's a bit windy, right?

468
00:18:17,552 --> 00:18:18,652
Do you want to play games?

469
00:18:18,652 --> 00:18:19,722
Games? Sounds good.

470
00:18:20,252 --> 00:18:21,992
I do want to play Halli Galli. It's been a while.

471
00:18:21,992 --> 00:18:22,992
Let's play it then.

472
00:18:23,362 --> 00:18:25,232
- This...
- Gosh, it's been so long.

473
00:18:25,492 --> 00:18:26,592
I forgot how to play this game.

474
00:18:27,832 --> 00:18:29,932
(Halli Galli)

475
00:18:32,932 --> 00:18:34,632
- Are they playing games?
- That's...

476
00:18:34,632 --> 00:18:36,872
But you end up touching each other's hands.

477
00:18:36,872 --> 00:18:38,072
- Right.
- Halli Galli.

478
00:18:38,072 --> 00:18:39,542
If you like that person, it's about touching hands.

479
00:18:39,542 --> 00:18:40,972
- Right.
- But if you don't like that person,

480
00:18:40,972 --> 00:18:42,012
- it's just a game.
- Yes.

481
00:18:42,582 --> 00:18:45,282
If you're interested in someone, that game is the perfect chance.

482
00:18:45,382 --> 00:18:47,712
And it's Halli Galli of all games.

483
00:18:48,452 --> 00:18:49,522
They should've played Jenga.

484
00:18:51,482 --> 00:18:53,522
You show the card like this, right?

485
00:18:53,522 --> 00:18:54,992
Yes. Right. And I have to...

486
00:18:56,222 --> 00:18:57,792
- show it like this.
- Wait.

487
00:18:58,292 --> 00:18:59,362
You startled me.

488
00:18:59,432 --> 00:19:01,062
- My gosh. Let's do it again.
- Okay.

489
00:19:01,062 --> 00:19:02,062
(Scrunching up)

490
00:19:07,872 --> 00:19:08,872
Wait.

491
00:19:08,872 --> 00:19:10,972
Oh, no. Look at them.

492
00:19:11,242 --> 00:19:12,742
Their hands touched on the bell.

493
00:19:12,742 --> 00:19:15,112
Wait. He just scrunched up his nose.

494
00:19:15,212 --> 00:19:16,682
- Yes.
- And their hands touched too.

495
00:19:18,012 --> 00:19:19,482
"Why are you breathing like that?"

496
00:19:20,012 --> 00:19:21,212
"Why did you cover your mouth just now?"

497
00:19:21,212 --> 00:19:22,752
"Why is your smile so beautiful?"

498
00:19:22,752 --> 00:19:24,052
He totally brought this upon himself. This is...

499
00:19:24,482 --> 00:19:25,922
Guys, stop playing the game.

500
00:19:29,962 --> 00:19:31,092
Do you go first?

501
00:19:31,192 --> 00:19:33,692
- I think so.
- Okay. I got it.

502
00:19:34,432 --> 00:19:35,902
Gosh, this isn't easy.

503
00:19:37,402 --> 00:19:39,032
- Are you angry?
- No.

504
00:19:39,732 --> 00:19:40,732
(Flinching)

505
00:19:41,602 --> 00:19:43,342
(Nervous)

506
00:19:43,342 --> 00:19:44,372
I'm scared.

507
00:19:47,012 --> 00:19:48,012
You...

508
00:19:48,012 --> 00:19:50,112
(She makes a mistake.)

509
00:19:51,952 --> 00:19:53,782
- Are you a competitive type?
- This is so annoying.

510
00:19:54,182 --> 00:19:56,182
- What?
- Are you a competitive type?

511
00:19:56,282 --> 00:19:58,252
- How did you know?
- I'm one of them too.

512
00:19:58,252 --> 00:19:59,252
- I can tell. Yes.
- Really?

513
00:19:59,252 --> 00:20:00,392
- Really?
- Yes.

514
00:20:00,522 --> 00:20:01,962
Aren't I really bad at this...

515
00:20:01,962 --> 00:20:03,592
when I can be so competitive?

516
00:20:07,332 --> 00:20:11,602
(Meanwhile, Jong Eun comes back after a hospital appointment.)

517
00:20:20,342 --> 00:20:23,282
(He brings back a bag of prescribed medicine.)

518
00:20:23,912 --> 00:20:26,212
- Hey. Hello.
- Hi.

519
00:20:26,312 --> 00:20:27,482
How was the doctor's appointment?

520
00:20:27,782 --> 00:20:29,852
- Right. It was today.
- You look very tired.

521
00:20:29,852 --> 00:20:30,852
Right.

522
00:20:31,282 --> 00:20:32,652
I was there since morning.

523
00:20:33,092 --> 00:20:34,122
What were you up to?

524
00:20:34,522 --> 00:20:37,222
- Oh, us? We went to buy bread.
- We had bread and milk.

525
00:20:37,222 --> 00:20:38,422
Do you want some bread?

526
00:20:38,632 --> 00:20:40,062
- Yes. We got a lot of good bread.
- What bread?

527
00:20:40,062 --> 00:20:41,392
- I see.
- Yes. We bought bread.

528
00:20:41,392 --> 00:20:42,562
- Did you two go?
- Yes.

529
00:20:43,602 --> 00:20:44,732
- I see.
- It's just us in the House.

530
00:20:44,732 --> 00:20:45,872
Yes. It's just us in the House.

531
00:20:45,872 --> 00:20:46,872
- Really?
- Yes.

532
00:20:46,872 --> 00:20:48,032
So we were...

533
00:20:48,032 --> 00:20:49,642
- We didn't know what to do.
- We were like, "What should we do?"

534
00:20:49,642 --> 00:20:51,702
- I asked him if he wanted to go.
- Yes. We bought bread.

535
00:20:54,012 --> 00:20:55,282
You look so tired.

536
00:20:55,282 --> 00:20:56,942
- No. I'm good.
- I...

537
00:20:59,282 --> 00:21:01,082
I also get tired after visiting the hospital.

538
00:21:01,182 --> 00:21:02,822
Well, I'm good.

539
00:21:03,582 --> 00:21:05,722
- I'll go and wash up.
- Okay.

540
00:21:05,722 --> 00:21:07,092
(Jong Eun looks more exhausted than usual.)

541
00:21:09,292 --> 00:21:11,692
(Worried)

542
00:21:11,692 --> 00:21:14,492
Well, the thing is, I was still...

543
00:21:14,492 --> 00:21:16,362
interested in Seon Ho.

544
00:21:16,462 --> 00:21:18,902
I was quite curious about him...

545
00:21:19,002 --> 00:21:21,502
when we first started talking.

546
00:21:21,832 --> 00:21:22,842
How should I put it?

547
00:21:24,342 --> 00:21:26,142
After seeing Jong Eun,

548
00:21:26,572 --> 00:21:29,682
it was like getting shot with an arrow in the heart.

549
00:21:29,782 --> 00:21:31,512
I did feel guilty for some reason.

550
00:21:31,512 --> 00:21:32,852
I think it was because...

551
00:21:33,112 --> 00:21:35,522
I kept having feelings for Jong Eun.

552
00:21:35,722 --> 00:21:38,822
So it was uncomfortable when it was the three of us.

553
00:21:39,922 --> 00:21:41,392
Right.

554
00:21:41,392 --> 00:21:43,322
My goodness. I guess...

555
00:21:43,322 --> 00:21:45,532
Ro Bin really likes Jong Eun.

556
00:21:45,532 --> 00:21:46,592
She can't give him the wrong idea.

557
00:21:46,592 --> 00:21:47,662
- She can't give him the wrong idea.
- Right.

558
00:21:47,662 --> 00:21:49,362
Of course, it bothers Ro Bin.

559
00:21:51,202 --> 00:21:53,132
(Seon Ho comes to see Jong Eun.)

560
00:21:53,432 --> 00:21:54,472
(Smiling)

561
00:21:55,772 --> 00:21:57,702
Why do you keep looking at me like that?

562
00:21:57,802 --> 00:21:58,942
Did you have fun?

563
00:21:58,942 --> 00:22:00,842
We just bought bread and came back. That was it.

564
00:22:01,412 --> 00:22:02,682
Did you guys talk a lot?

565
00:22:02,912 --> 00:22:04,582
- We did.
- How was it?

566
00:22:04,812 --> 00:22:06,482
Why? Are you jealous?

567
00:22:06,482 --> 00:22:08,982
- What? No.
- Are you jealous?

568
00:22:09,352 --> 00:22:10,922
No. I was just curious.

569
00:22:14,292 --> 00:22:16,662
Then you, Ro Bin, and I... The three of us...

570
00:22:17,192 --> 00:22:18,692
- didn't go out on a date?
- Yes.

571
00:22:18,692 --> 00:22:20,132
Should we prepare dinner together?

572
00:22:20,232 --> 00:22:21,232
Sounds good.

573
00:22:22,062 --> 00:22:23,132
I feel lonely.

574
00:22:24,662 --> 00:22:25,932
Or...

575
00:22:26,672 --> 00:22:28,232
she's there.

576
00:22:28,402 --> 00:22:30,642
We've been on a date before.

577
00:22:31,902 --> 00:22:34,212
I don't like her that way.

578
00:22:34,212 --> 00:22:35,812
- You don't?
- No.

579
00:22:37,642 --> 00:22:38,712
My gosh, wait.

580
00:22:38,712 --> 00:22:40,012
(Disappointed)

581
00:22:40,852 --> 00:22:42,022
Oh, no.

582
00:22:42,022 --> 00:22:43,482
Gosh, poor Ro Bin.

583
00:22:43,482 --> 00:22:44,882
I see.

584
00:22:44,982 --> 00:22:46,552
This is awful.

585
00:22:47,752 --> 00:22:50,562
I've gone on a date with Ro Bin...

586
00:22:50,562 --> 00:22:52,132
- and Min Young.
- Yes.

587
00:22:52,232 --> 00:22:55,932
Even though Min Young and I didn't talk much,

588
00:22:55,932 --> 00:22:58,672
I still had more fun with her.

589
00:22:59,232 --> 00:23:01,372
Right. That could happen. Yes.

590
00:23:01,832 --> 00:23:04,702
So I don't know.

591
00:23:06,172 --> 00:23:07,242
Gosh, this is hard.

592
00:23:08,042 --> 00:23:09,782
How was it for you? You guys talked.

593
00:23:10,282 --> 00:23:11,482
- Ro Bin?
- Yes.

594
00:23:12,112 --> 00:23:13,512
You wanted to talk to her too.

595
00:23:14,112 --> 00:23:15,112
Yes.

596
00:23:15,682 --> 00:23:16,782
I think that was enough.

597
00:23:17,782 --> 00:23:19,252
- I mean it.
- What do you mean?

598
00:23:19,252 --> 00:23:20,522
We talked enough.

599
00:23:20,722 --> 00:23:21,922
I was like, "I see."

600
00:23:22,722 --> 00:23:25,292
But I had more fun with Ye Ji.

601
00:23:25,592 --> 00:23:26,592
(Surprised)

602
00:23:26,592 --> 00:23:27,662
That was sudden!

603
00:23:27,662 --> 00:23:29,502
- What? Hold on. Play that again.
- Wait.

604
00:23:29,502 --> 00:23:30,732
- Wait.
- I'm sorry.

605
00:23:31,132 --> 00:23:33,072
- What is this? It was so random.
- Go back ten seconds.

606
00:23:33,072 --> 00:23:34,272
That was a definite answer, wasn't it?

607
00:23:34,272 --> 00:23:35,272
- Right.
- Yes.

608
00:23:36,542 --> 00:23:39,042
But I had more fun with Ye Ji.

609
00:23:41,072 --> 00:23:42,542
- Now...
- See? This is it.

610
00:23:42,542 --> 00:23:44,412
Seon Ho wanted to talk to...

611
00:23:44,412 --> 00:23:45,612
- everyone first.
- I see.

612
00:23:45,612 --> 00:23:47,682
Then it became clear to him that he was...

613
00:23:47,682 --> 00:23:48,882
- most interested in her.
- Yes.

614
00:23:48,882 --> 00:23:51,482
- No. He's not there yet.
- But just now...

615
00:23:51,482 --> 00:23:53,092
- He just had more fun with her.
- It was more fun.

616
00:23:53,092 --> 00:23:54,622
He had more fun with Ye Ji.

617
00:23:54,622 --> 00:23:56,292
That's all. He just had more fun.

618
00:23:56,992 --> 00:23:59,362
It's not, "I like her more."

619
00:23:59,362 --> 00:24:01,992
So he might have to get to know other people more.

620
00:24:02,062 --> 00:24:03,132
- I see. He has to...
- Or...

621
00:24:03,132 --> 00:24:04,562
- get to know other people more?
- That's right.

622
00:24:04,562 --> 00:24:05,832
I'm saying that's a possibility too.

623
00:24:05,832 --> 00:24:07,372
Now that he's gotten to know these two ladies,

624
00:24:07,632 --> 00:24:09,102
he might want to get to know other ladies more.

625
00:24:09,102 --> 00:24:10,472
- Right.
- He might have meant that too.

626
00:24:10,472 --> 00:24:13,012
- Did I lower my guard for a second?
- It's...

627
00:24:13,012 --> 00:24:14,012
- It's too soon to tell.
- Right?

628
00:24:14,012 --> 00:24:15,912
Right? I lowered my guard again.

629
00:24:17,512 --> 00:24:21,482
(It's hard to figure out where the guys stand for now.)

630
00:24:21,482 --> 00:24:22,482
I see.

631
00:24:23,722 --> 00:24:25,252
I just found out that there were flip-flops here.

632
00:24:25,252 --> 00:24:26,922
- I just found out too.
- Really?

633
00:24:26,922 --> 00:24:29,322
I see. You came here after seeing me come out.

634
00:24:29,322 --> 00:24:30,322
Yes.

635
00:24:30,492 --> 00:24:34,132
We might be able to see everyone coming home from here.

636
00:24:34,962 --> 00:24:37,432
You're right. They'll come up this way.

637
00:24:37,432 --> 00:24:40,332
We can sit here all day, Seon Ho.

638
00:24:40,332 --> 00:24:42,002
- "I see." - "Hey, you're home."

639
00:24:43,272 --> 00:24:44,272
It's cool here.

640
00:24:45,342 --> 00:24:46,372
It's much cooler here.

641
00:24:48,912 --> 00:24:52,952
(Jong Eun comes out to the balcony.)

642
00:24:55,582 --> 00:24:56,582
(Spotting them)

643
00:24:56,582 --> 00:24:57,782
- What are you doing?
- Come on down.

644
00:24:57,782 --> 00:24:58,952
Come down here.

645
00:25:02,492 --> 00:25:04,262
I'll look around over there and go down.

646
00:25:05,122 --> 00:25:06,162
Where?

647
00:25:15,972 --> 00:25:17,702
(Staring)

648
00:25:17,702 --> 00:25:20,172
He's standing there like the main character of a drama.

649
00:25:24,142 --> 00:25:28,112
(Ro Bin can't take her eyes off Jong Eun.)

650
00:25:47,372 --> 00:25:49,602
(Beckoning over)

651
00:25:49,902 --> 00:25:52,512
(Jong Eun misses Ro Bin beckoning him over.)

652
00:25:53,872 --> 00:25:56,212
Jong Eun. Come on down.

653
00:25:56,882 --> 00:25:57,882
Okay.

654
00:26:05,492 --> 00:26:07,922
- Are you not having bread?
- What?

655
00:26:07,922 --> 00:26:08,992
Shall we go upstairs now?

656
00:26:08,992 --> 00:26:10,262
Go upstairs now?

657
00:26:11,662 --> 00:26:12,932
We're joking.

658
00:26:13,462 --> 00:26:14,992
What should we make for dinner tonight?

659
00:26:15,602 --> 00:26:17,332
Fried rice and pork belly.

660
00:26:17,332 --> 00:26:19,602
I'm thinking about making one of those.

661
00:26:19,602 --> 00:26:20,872
Right now?

662
00:26:21,902 --> 00:26:23,172
Have you eaten?

663
00:26:23,502 --> 00:26:25,402
- Yes.
- You didn't have lunch.

664
00:26:25,402 --> 00:26:26,512
- Lunch...
- Yes.

665
00:26:26,512 --> 00:26:27,612
I had lunch.

666
00:26:28,412 --> 00:26:29,582
What did you have for lunch?

667
00:26:29,582 --> 00:26:31,182
- Lunch?
- We had some bread.

668
00:26:31,182 --> 00:26:32,182
Bread.

669
00:26:32,182 --> 00:26:34,212
- Do you want some bread?
- That would be nice.

670
00:26:34,212 --> 00:26:35,682
- Shall we go and eat that?
- Okay.

671
00:26:35,682 --> 00:26:37,182
While eating bread, I'll...

672
00:26:38,482 --> 00:26:40,452
- It's already 6pm.
- I know.

673
00:26:40,452 --> 00:26:41,692
That's right. It's an awkward time.

674
00:26:41,692 --> 00:26:43,492
Can you eat dinner after having some bread?

675
00:26:43,492 --> 00:26:44,592
Right.

676
00:26:45,062 --> 00:26:46,662
Pork belly?

677
00:26:46,662 --> 00:26:47,892
- Let's have pork belly.
- Yes.

678
00:26:47,892 --> 00:26:48,902
Yes.

679
00:26:48,902 --> 00:26:50,862
(While they decide to prepare dinner)

680
00:26:51,002 --> 00:26:52,232
You've arrived at your destination.

681
00:26:52,232 --> 00:26:53,472
If you get used to it...

682
00:26:53,832 --> 00:26:56,072
(Ye Ji and Do Gon are back from their date)

683
00:26:56,272 --> 00:26:57,542
It's the House.

684
00:27:03,882 --> 00:27:05,282
Thank you.

685
00:27:08,552 --> 00:27:11,022
- I'll get changed.
- Okay.

686
00:27:29,242 --> 00:27:30,302
(Pausing)

687
00:27:32,842 --> 00:27:36,612
(Staring)

688
00:27:39,882 --> 00:27:41,252
She's looking for him.

689
00:27:41,252 --> 00:27:42,582
She'd have been so curious.

690
00:27:42,582 --> 00:27:43,652
Right.

691
00:27:43,652 --> 00:27:46,422
She thought about Seon Ho throughout her date.

692
00:27:46,422 --> 00:27:48,852
She'd be curious to know what he's doing.

693
00:27:54,032 --> 00:27:57,062
I think I went around looking for Seon Ho...

694
00:27:57,062 --> 00:27:58,662
as soon as I arrived.

695
00:27:58,662 --> 00:28:01,032
I wanted to talk to him. I wanted to ask him...

696
00:28:01,032 --> 00:28:03,142
about what happened at the House today...

697
00:28:03,142 --> 00:28:04,572
and how he spent his time.

698
00:28:04,572 --> 00:28:06,412
I was curious to know how his day was.

699
00:28:09,712 --> 00:28:11,582
(Glancing)

700
00:28:17,652 --> 00:28:23,022
(She's curious to know about Seon Ho's day.)

701
00:28:24,262 --> 00:28:30,102
(The three people are still together.)

702
00:28:30,402 --> 00:28:32,002
It's really funny.

703
00:28:32,672 --> 00:28:34,472
- Hey, Do Gon.
- Hey.

704
00:28:34,472 --> 00:28:36,142
When did you get back?

705
00:28:37,142 --> 00:28:39,342
- Is someone here?
- Is someone here?

706
00:28:40,172 --> 00:28:41,442
Where are they?

707
00:28:41,642 --> 00:28:42,742
- Wait.
- Wait.

708
00:28:45,042 --> 00:28:47,082
Did you have dinner today?

709
00:28:47,382 --> 00:28:48,812
I had something simple.

710
00:28:48,812 --> 00:28:50,152
I wanted to eat here.

711
00:28:50,152 --> 00:28:53,322
We're going to have some pork belly.

712
00:28:53,322 --> 00:28:54,652
- Pork belly?
- Yes.

713
00:28:55,592 --> 00:28:56,662
(Glancing)

714
00:28:58,422 --> 00:29:00,432
(Waving)

715
00:29:03,762 --> 00:29:06,702
(They exchanged a quick hand wave.)

716
00:29:08,072 --> 00:29:09,542
He should just take care of her if he likes her.

717
00:29:09,542 --> 00:29:11,042
- Even a word.
- Just one word.

718
00:29:11,042 --> 00:29:12,572
- "You're back." - "You're back."

719
00:29:12,572 --> 00:29:13,572
Just those words.

720
00:29:13,572 --> 00:29:14,942
- He's still inexperienced.
- No.

721
00:29:14,942 --> 00:29:16,482
I think he may be acting that way...

722
00:29:16,482 --> 00:29:19,152
because he feels weird.

723
00:29:19,152 --> 00:29:20,382
Is he a little upset?

724
00:29:20,382 --> 00:29:21,782
He's not upset...

725
00:29:21,782 --> 00:29:23,282
He's he acting like he's upset?

726
00:29:25,482 --> 00:29:27,452
He's good at pretending...

727
00:29:27,452 --> 00:29:28,992
it doesn't bother him.

728
00:29:28,992 --> 00:29:30,392
That's right.

729
00:29:33,162 --> 00:29:34,562
That's when I knew...

730
00:29:34,562 --> 00:29:38,032
that Ye Ji went out on a date with Do Gon.

731
00:29:38,032 --> 00:29:40,432
I felt...

732
00:29:40,432 --> 00:29:42,202
a little weird.

733
00:29:42,202 --> 00:29:43,502
"What's going on?"

734
00:29:43,502 --> 00:29:46,942
Yesterday, she went on a date with me, but today, with another...

735
00:29:46,942 --> 00:29:48,572
It was weird.

736
00:29:48,572 --> 00:29:50,882
I had mixed feelings.

737
00:29:58,622 --> 00:30:00,252
I met Seon Ho.

738
00:30:00,252 --> 00:30:02,792
My head hurt from all the thoughts...

739
00:30:02,792 --> 00:30:06,062
when I tried to talk to him.

740
00:30:07,162 --> 00:30:08,492
(Peeping)

741
00:30:10,102 --> 00:30:12,132
- What are you doing?
- We're going to play a game.

742
00:30:12,132 --> 00:30:13,372
This...

743
00:30:15,232 --> 00:30:17,072
- Do you want to play with us?
- Yes.

744
00:30:17,802 --> 00:30:19,442
I'll get changed then.

745
00:30:19,442 --> 00:30:20,712
Do you know how to play this?

746
00:30:22,812 --> 00:30:26,012
(A moment later)

747
00:30:26,712 --> 00:30:27,882
(The four people decide to play a game.)

748
00:30:27,882 --> 00:30:29,852
Shall we decide on the penalty?

749
00:30:29,852 --> 00:30:31,322
What penalty should we get?

750
00:30:31,822 --> 00:30:33,022
Truth or Dare?

751
00:30:34,192 --> 00:30:35,392
(This is interesting.)

752
00:30:35,392 --> 00:30:37,162
- They're going to play a game.
- Truth or Dare?

753
00:30:37,422 --> 00:30:39,232
That's good for Ye Ji.

754
00:30:39,232 --> 00:30:41,492
- Yes.
- She'll get to know the truth.

755
00:30:41,492 --> 00:30:42,762
That's right.

756
00:30:42,762 --> 00:30:44,202
(Focusing)

757
00:30:45,062 --> 00:30:47,632
(Truth or Dare will reveal how everyone really feels.)

758
00:30:47,632 --> 00:30:49,972
When it falls,

759
00:30:49,972 --> 00:30:52,742
someone will ask you a question, and you'll say the truth.

760
00:30:53,142 --> 00:30:54,542
You have to be honest.

761
00:30:55,512 --> 00:30:57,182
(Getting nervous)

762
00:30:58,382 --> 00:31:00,052
Okay.

763
00:31:00,052 --> 00:31:01,052
Are you all fine with that?

764
00:31:01,052 --> 00:31:02,252
Okay.

765
00:31:02,252 --> 00:31:04,152
- Okay.
- No lying. Be honest.

766
00:31:04,152 --> 00:31:05,252
Okay.

767
00:31:07,822 --> 00:31:10,592
(The truth game begins with a strange sense of tension.)

768
00:31:11,162 --> 00:31:13,292
Rock-paper-scissors.

769
00:31:13,292 --> 00:31:14,592
- Rock-paper-scissors.
- Rock-paper-scissors.

770
00:31:14,592 --> 00:31:16,002
- Yes.
- I'm last.

771
00:31:16,202 --> 00:31:18,332
Isn't going first a disadvantage?

772
00:31:18,332 --> 00:31:20,272
(Jong Eun will start.)

773
00:31:21,902 --> 00:31:23,402
(Pulling)

774
00:31:23,402 --> 00:31:26,012
(He smoothly succeeds.)

775
00:31:26,012 --> 00:31:28,112
(Second up is Do Gon.)

776
00:31:28,642 --> 00:31:30,182
(Shaking)

777
00:31:30,182 --> 00:31:31,282
Hold on.

778
00:31:31,542 --> 00:31:32,612
Already?

779
00:31:32,852 --> 00:31:34,312
Hold on.

780
00:31:35,452 --> 00:31:37,222
(Hitting trouble from the start)

781
00:31:37,922 --> 00:31:39,492
I think it's already over.

782
00:31:39,492 --> 00:31:41,922
- Let's think of a question.
- Okay.

783
00:31:43,922 --> 00:31:45,492
(Shaking)

784
00:31:46,092 --> 00:31:47,092
(Do Gon's tower is falling.)

785
00:31:47,092 --> 00:31:48,792
This is already happening on the second turn?

786
00:31:49,562 --> 00:31:50,662
This is so funny.

787
00:31:50,662 --> 00:31:53,202
I'm so bad at this game.

788
00:31:55,102 --> 00:31:56,102
(Do Gon gets the penalty for the first round.)

789
00:31:56,102 --> 00:31:57,642
What should we ask him?

790
00:31:58,842 --> 00:32:00,612
(He's devastated.)

791
00:32:01,742 --> 00:32:03,612
Okay. Ask away.

792
00:32:04,982 --> 00:32:07,152
(Feeling nervous)

793
00:32:09,982 --> 00:32:13,422
(There's a sudden silence.)

794
00:32:15,222 --> 00:32:17,222
(Glancing)

795
00:32:20,692 --> 00:32:22,462
Did you find someone you like?

796
00:32:24,102 --> 00:32:26,872
(She's flustered.)

797
00:32:27,132 --> 00:32:28,572
(Glancing)

798
00:32:34,142 --> 00:32:35,812
There's someone...

799
00:32:36,382 --> 00:32:37,412
I'm interested in right now.

800
00:32:38,482 --> 00:32:39,482
(Nodding)

801
00:32:41,212 --> 00:32:42,212
Right.

802
00:32:42,582 --> 00:32:44,782
(Nodding)

803
00:32:44,922 --> 00:32:46,722
(They move right into Round 2.)

804
00:32:49,762 --> 00:32:50,862
Wait.

805
00:32:52,862 --> 00:32:54,562
- Already?
- That happens.

806
00:32:55,362 --> 00:32:56,962
It's your turn now.

807
00:32:58,862 --> 00:32:59,932
Wait.

808
00:33:00,902 --> 00:33:03,302
(Shaking)

809
00:33:07,772 --> 00:33:08,942
What?

810
00:33:09,112 --> 00:33:10,182
No way.

811
00:33:10,682 --> 00:33:12,042
He's trembling.

812
00:33:12,042 --> 00:33:13,182
It's falling.

813
00:33:13,182 --> 00:33:14,482
It fell!

814
00:33:15,752 --> 00:33:18,022
Okay!

815
00:33:18,022 --> 00:33:19,152
- That's right!
- It fell!

816
00:33:19,152 --> 00:33:20,652
This is what I'm talking about.

817
00:33:20,652 --> 00:33:21,892
Don't say, "No comment."

818
00:33:21,892 --> 00:33:23,192
Who'll be asking?

819
00:33:23,192 --> 00:33:24,322
Will they take turns asking?

820
00:33:24,322 --> 00:33:26,892
- Ye Ji will be dying to know.
- Just ask away.

821
00:33:29,962 --> 00:33:32,232
It's your turn.

822
00:33:32,432 --> 00:33:33,872
- This is fair.
- Right.

823
00:33:33,872 --> 00:33:35,672
Nice.

824
00:33:35,672 --> 00:33:37,602
Let's ask him.

825
00:33:40,042 --> 00:33:41,742
What should we ask him?

826
00:33:43,282 --> 00:33:44,612
(Feeling anxious)

827
00:33:44,612 --> 00:33:46,052
I'll ask first.

828
00:33:46,052 --> 00:33:47,112
Okay.

829
00:33:48,012 --> 00:33:51,422
Tell us which date...

830
00:33:51,422 --> 00:33:54,052
you've enjoyed the most so far.

831
00:33:57,092 --> 00:33:58,622
That's a meaningful question.

832
00:33:59,392 --> 00:34:01,062
- That was a good question.
- That was good.

833
00:34:01,062 --> 00:34:03,262
- Ye Ji likes it.
- Well done.

834
00:34:03,262 --> 00:34:04,332
Nice.

835
00:34:04,332 --> 00:34:05,902
I hope he tells them honestly.

836
00:34:06,602 --> 00:34:08,202
- It's okay, right?
- It's good.

837
00:34:08,202 --> 00:34:10,342
- You're good at asking questions.
- Nice.

838
00:34:11,142 --> 00:34:13,742
This is what makes the game fun.

839
00:34:14,312 --> 00:34:15,712
It's so difficult.

840
00:34:18,012 --> 00:34:21,082
You enjoyed the date...

841
00:34:21,082 --> 00:34:22,952
in the morning or afternoon of a certain day.

842
00:34:23,452 --> 00:34:24,682
That's how you should say it.

843
00:34:27,592 --> 00:34:29,492
Can I take some time to think about it?

844
00:34:30,262 --> 00:34:32,892
You seem very nervous.

845
00:34:36,462 --> 00:34:39,672
(She's curious.)

846
00:34:44,442 --> 00:34:47,412
I think I liked yesterday's date.

847
00:34:49,882 --> 00:34:52,512
(Seon Ho went on two dates yesterday.)

848
00:34:53,212 --> 00:34:56,352
(His first date was with Min Young.)

849
00:34:57,882 --> 00:35:01,252
(His second date was with Ye Ji.)

850
00:35:03,292 --> 00:35:04,992
One of those two?

851
00:35:04,992 --> 00:35:06,032
- Seriously...
- He is...

852
00:35:06,032 --> 00:35:07,532
not saying who it is.

853
00:35:07,532 --> 00:35:09,562
Who answers it like that?

854
00:35:09,562 --> 00:35:11,562
Hold on. Why does he always...

855
00:35:11,562 --> 00:35:13,932
leave a 50 percent chance?

856
00:35:17,442 --> 00:35:21,572
(Which date left an impression on Seon Ho?)

857
00:35:23,542 --> 00:35:24,682
- Rock-paper-scissors!
- Rock-paper-scissors!

858
00:35:25,212 --> 00:35:26,312
Rock-paper-scissors.

859
00:35:26,552 --> 00:35:28,052
- Rock-paper-scissors!
- Why am I always last?

860
00:35:28,882 --> 00:35:29,882
Wait.

861
00:35:29,922 --> 00:35:31,952
- Hold on.
- You got the wrong one.

862
00:35:32,452 --> 00:35:34,592
- Can I use this hand to do this?
- Sure.

863
00:35:34,592 --> 00:35:35,952
(Tapping)

864
00:35:36,892 --> 00:35:38,322
- It's somewhat...
- Wait...

865
00:35:38,322 --> 00:35:39,632
This is driving me crazy.

866
00:35:40,062 --> 00:35:41,232
(Pushing)

867
00:35:41,792 --> 00:35:43,062
It's going to fall.

868
00:35:45,302 --> 00:35:46,572
Seriously.

869
00:35:48,332 --> 00:35:49,542
(Smiling)

870
00:35:49,542 --> 00:35:51,472
This part is just shaking.

871
00:35:51,472 --> 00:35:54,042
This part seems out.

872
00:35:56,282 --> 00:35:58,442
(Staring)

873
00:35:59,582 --> 00:36:00,912
Please.

874
00:36:01,782 --> 00:36:03,682
- You're almost there.
- The corner part is stuck.

875
00:36:03,682 --> 00:36:04,852
(Sharp eyes)

876
00:36:04,852 --> 00:36:06,152
(With a twisting skill)

877
00:36:06,152 --> 00:36:07,192
Hold on.

878
00:36:07,752 --> 00:36:08,752
Yes.

879
00:36:08,752 --> 00:36:11,092
(She fails.)

880
00:36:11,092 --> 00:36:12,592
You were so close.

881
00:36:12,932 --> 00:36:13,992
What a shame.

882
00:36:15,992 --> 00:36:17,102
You're good.

883
00:36:17,432 --> 00:36:18,462
I was so close.

884
00:36:18,462 --> 00:36:19,902
- Let's put these on top.
- Yes.

885
00:36:21,102 --> 00:36:25,002
(It's time to ask Ye Ji.)

886
00:36:26,972 --> 00:36:29,882
How many people are you interested in?

887
00:36:30,042 --> 00:36:31,142
How many people?

888
00:36:32,082 --> 00:36:33,882
(Thinking)

889
00:36:43,092 --> 00:36:44,122
Two.

890
00:36:44,662 --> 00:36:45,692
Two.

891
00:36:51,762 --> 00:36:52,802
I'll ask.

892
00:36:54,272 --> 00:36:56,102
The two people you're interested in...

893
00:36:57,302 --> 00:36:58,402
are here.

894
00:36:59,572 --> 00:37:01,072
- Are they here or not?
- Here?

895
00:37:06,752 --> 00:37:07,882
That's a strong one.

896
00:37:09,282 --> 00:37:10,552
This makes it fun, doesn't it?

897
00:37:10,552 --> 00:37:11,622
It's strong.

898
00:37:12,622 --> 00:37:15,492
But what's the definition of being interested in someone?

899
00:37:16,662 --> 00:37:18,022
- Someone you're drawn to.
- Okay.

900
00:37:22,862 --> 00:37:23,862
They're here.

901
00:37:25,562 --> 00:37:26,732
Okay.

902
00:37:27,680 --> 00:37:28,780
(Glancing)

903
00:37:29,450 --> 00:37:32,320
(It's Seon Ho's turn to ask.)

904
00:37:34,306 --> 00:37:35,806
Did you enjoy today's date?

905
00:37:38,046 --> 00:37:39,306
- Today's date?
- Yes.

906
00:37:40,516 --> 00:37:44,246
(Seon Ho asked if she enjoyed the date with Do Gon.)

907
00:37:44,816 --> 00:37:46,216
- Are you asking if I enjoyed it?
- Yes.

908
00:37:47,216 --> 00:37:49,186
(Nodding)

909
00:37:50,856 --> 00:37:51,956
All right.

910
00:37:53,096 --> 00:37:54,096
(Exclaiming)

911
00:37:54,096 --> 00:37:56,226
- What?
- That's just about this.

912
00:37:56,666 --> 00:37:58,926
The answer isn't important for that question.

913
00:37:59,736 --> 00:38:00,936
He was expressing himself.

914
00:38:01,736 --> 00:38:03,966
- Really?
- He meant, "I'm bothered by it."

915
00:38:03,966 --> 00:38:05,066
That's right.

916
00:38:05,636 --> 00:38:08,606
- Of course she'll say it was fun.
- Right.

917
00:38:08,806 --> 00:38:09,946
That question itself...

918
00:38:09,946 --> 00:38:11,576
sounds like, "Did you enjoy today's date?"

919
00:38:11,746 --> 00:38:13,576
- "It's bothering me." - That's the nuance of it.

920
00:38:13,976 --> 00:38:15,246
"Did you enjoy today's date?"

921
00:38:15,546 --> 00:38:17,146
- I get it.
- He was expressing that in a way.

922
00:38:17,146 --> 00:38:18,216
Right.

923
00:38:20,056 --> 00:38:23,086
Ye Ji was asked if there was someone there...

924
00:38:23,226 --> 00:38:26,226
that she was interested in.

925
00:38:26,226 --> 00:38:27,726
She said yes...

926
00:38:27,856 --> 00:38:29,196
and that there were two people.

927
00:38:29,766 --> 00:38:32,696
I thought that would be Do Gon and me.

928
00:38:33,836 --> 00:38:35,336
Do Gon is older than me.

929
00:38:35,496 --> 00:38:38,306
He's a stable person,

930
00:38:38,866 --> 00:38:40,106
and he's cool.

931
00:38:40,376 --> 00:38:41,536
So...

932
00:38:42,846 --> 00:38:44,476
I became conscious of that.

933
00:38:47,616 --> 00:38:53,386
(He started becoming conscious of another man.)

934
00:38:54,516 --> 00:38:57,386
After revealing our jobs yesterday,

935
00:38:57,386 --> 00:38:58,386
Yes.

936
00:38:58,386 --> 00:39:00,296
I wanted to take a picture...

937
00:39:00,996 --> 00:39:02,826
with our great actress.

938
00:39:03,396 --> 00:39:04,826
I heard there's...

939
00:39:05,166 --> 00:39:07,966
a photo booth where you can take four-cut photos.

940
00:39:07,966 --> 00:39:09,096
That would be nice.

941
00:39:09,266 --> 00:39:11,336
I rarely take selfies.

942
00:39:11,436 --> 00:39:12,536
- What is this place?
- It's a photo booth.

943
00:39:12,536 --> 00:39:13,806
(Ryun Gi wanted to take pictures with Na Young.)

944
00:39:13,806 --> 00:39:14,906
This is amazing.

945
00:39:16,006 --> 00:39:18,376
It's so vintage and nice here.

946
00:39:19,346 --> 00:39:21,116
Come to the left side.

947
00:39:22,886 --> 00:39:24,046
Don't you need to check yourself in the mirror?

948
00:39:24,046 --> 00:39:25,216
You have to check now.

949
00:39:25,216 --> 00:39:26,556
- Why?
- They won't give you time.

950
00:39:27,416 --> 00:39:29,656
- I don't need to.
- What's with that confidence?

951
00:39:30,526 --> 00:39:31,956
You have such a small face.

952
00:39:31,956 --> 00:39:33,926
- My face will look so big.
- Should I stand in front?

953
00:39:35,826 --> 00:39:36,966
Where should I look at?

954
00:39:37,166 --> 00:39:38,366
It's going to look pretty.

955
00:39:50,546 --> 00:39:51,646
Let's smile.

956
00:40:02,586 --> 00:40:06,856
(The excitement of their first date was captured in the photos.)

957
00:40:07,756 --> 00:40:09,126
- That's nice.
- They look nice.

958
00:40:09,126 --> 00:40:10,266
- That's amazing.
- What's that place?

959
00:40:10,266 --> 00:40:11,396
- Where is that place?
- Where is that place?

960
00:40:11,726 --> 00:40:13,936
(Exchanging looks)

961
00:40:13,936 --> 00:40:15,096
Shall we go there?

962
00:40:16,266 --> 00:40:17,706
- Shall we take pictures there?
- Do you want to go out on a date?

963
00:40:19,036 --> 00:40:20,136
We'll be doing this.

964
00:40:20,136 --> 00:40:21,476
(Yong Hwa and DK are matched for a date.)

965
00:40:23,846 --> 00:40:24,906
This is so cute.

966
00:40:25,046 --> 00:40:26,246
- Do you like it?
- Yes.

967
00:40:28,046 --> 00:40:29,446
You know,

968
00:40:30,816 --> 00:40:32,286
when I look at you,

969
00:40:32,286 --> 00:40:34,686
you really have a small face.

970
00:40:35,156 --> 00:40:36,686
But I also had a small face.

971
00:40:36,956 --> 00:40:38,686
It's really small.

972
00:40:38,956 --> 00:40:40,626
- What are you talking about?
- That's a relief.

973
00:40:40,626 --> 00:40:42,696
You said you were going to stand in front,

974
00:40:42,696 --> 00:40:44,296
but you leaned to the wall.

975
00:40:44,296 --> 00:40:47,336
I was worried because your actions...

976
00:40:47,336 --> 00:40:48,436
and words didn't match.

977
00:40:48,436 --> 00:40:50,206
- Did you feel betrayed?
- Yes.

978
00:40:50,506 --> 00:40:52,006
You're the one with a small face,

979
00:40:52,006 --> 00:40:53,636
and you keep telling me that I have a small face.

980
00:40:54,036 --> 00:40:56,076
Yours is really small.

981
00:40:57,776 --> 00:41:01,576
(After a walk with some easy conversation,)

982
00:41:02,376 --> 00:41:06,656
(they arrive at the date spot chosen by Ryun Gi.)

983
00:41:06,656 --> 00:41:07,686
What is this place?

984
00:41:07,986 --> 00:41:10,756
I heard the owner takes these photos...

985
00:41:10,756 --> 00:41:12,686
and turns them into postcards to sell here.

986
00:41:12,756 --> 00:41:13,856
That's amazing.

987
00:41:15,496 --> 00:41:17,066
They're so pretty.

988
00:41:18,866 --> 00:41:20,836
(They decided to write postcards to each other.)

989
00:41:20,836 --> 00:41:21,836
This one?

990
00:41:22,036 --> 00:41:24,166
I really like this one.

991
00:41:24,166 --> 00:41:26,936
(Na Young chose one right away.)

992
00:41:29,106 --> 00:41:32,816
(Ryun Gi takes his time to choose a postcard.)

993
00:41:35,276 --> 00:41:36,546
I'll start writing first.

994
00:41:42,356 --> 00:41:43,826
- Did you pick one?
- Yes.

995
00:41:44,456 --> 00:41:45,956
I like the mood here.

996
00:41:46,596 --> 00:41:48,326
The mood of these two people.

997
00:41:48,326 --> 00:41:49,356
The mood?

998
00:41:50,226 --> 00:41:52,696
- They seem so comfortable.
- Yes. It's so beautiful.

999
00:41:54,166 --> 00:41:55,536
What are you going to write about?

1000
00:41:57,936 --> 00:41:59,366
What should I write about?

1001
00:42:02,336 --> 00:42:04,776
Your first impression...

1002
00:42:05,306 --> 00:42:07,576
- And how I feel today?
- How they're different.

1003
00:42:09,716 --> 00:42:10,916
Okay.

1004
00:42:12,486 --> 00:42:13,586
Don't look.

1005
00:42:20,896 --> 00:42:23,726
(They start writing postcards...)

1006
00:42:23,726 --> 00:42:26,796
(while reminiscing about their first meeting.)

1007
00:42:28,196 --> 00:42:33,376
(How have their first impressions of each other...)

1008
00:42:35,206 --> 00:42:40,376
(changed since then?)

1009
00:42:44,016 --> 00:42:45,246
I'm done.

1010
00:42:50,826 --> 00:42:51,826
I'm done.

1011
00:42:52,826 --> 00:42:53,896
Shall we exchange them?

1012
00:42:54,096 --> 00:42:55,556
Right now? I feel shy.

1013
00:42:55,556 --> 00:42:57,326
Why? When else will we read them?

1014
00:42:57,326 --> 00:42:58,666
I want to read it now.

1015
00:43:02,596 --> 00:43:04,306
(They exchange the postcards they wrote for each other.)

1016
00:43:04,306 --> 00:43:05,666
This is how you wrote it.

1017
00:43:05,666 --> 00:43:07,706
(They exchange the postcards they wrote for each other.)

1018
00:43:09,136 --> 00:43:11,176
- Can I read it out loud?
- What?

1019
00:43:11,776 --> 00:43:12,846
No.

1020
00:43:12,846 --> 00:43:14,716
Can't I read it out loud?

1021
00:43:16,286 --> 00:43:17,286
Okay.

1022
00:43:17,286 --> 00:43:20,056
I happened to be the last person to walk in.

1023
00:43:21,186 --> 00:43:22,716
I thought, "I should walk in confidently."

1024
00:43:22,716 --> 00:43:25,026
"I met Ryun Gi for the first time when I greeted everyone."

1025
00:43:27,156 --> 00:43:29,326
"He's not really my type."

1026
00:43:31,096 --> 00:43:33,496
"He's someone who knows how to empathize with other people..."

1027
00:43:34,696 --> 00:43:37,766
"and take something away from them. He's a pure and humble person."

1028
00:43:39,436 --> 00:43:43,076
"He's an honest person who laughed and cried, and found his own way..."

1029
00:43:44,476 --> 00:43:47,346
"even through the difficult process."

1030
00:43:48,216 --> 00:43:51,516
I'm truly honored to have gotten to know you like this.

1031
00:43:51,516 --> 00:43:52,956
(I'm truly honored, Kim Ryun Gi.)

1032
00:43:53,156 --> 00:43:55,816
Thank you. You said such nice things.

1033
00:43:56,656 --> 00:43:57,826
This is really embarrassing.

1034
00:43:57,826 --> 00:43:59,926
- You're not crying, right?
- I almost cried.

1035
00:44:02,026 --> 00:44:03,666
When I first met Na Young,

1036
00:44:03,666 --> 00:44:06,096
I saw her as a bright and cheerful girl...

1037
00:44:06,436 --> 00:44:09,266
who brings positive energy to the people around her.

1038
00:44:10,206 --> 00:44:12,706
Sometimes, when she opens up and shares her honest...

1039
00:44:12,706 --> 00:44:14,476
and sincere thoughts,

1040
00:44:14,676 --> 00:44:16,606
I find her really charming.

1041
00:44:16,676 --> 00:44:17,846
You got that right.

1042
00:44:19,646 --> 00:44:21,246
I think her experiences and her thoughtful side...

1043
00:44:21,246 --> 00:44:23,416
are truly admirable,

1044
00:44:23,646 --> 00:44:26,556
so I hope more people get to see this side of her.

1045
00:44:26,716 --> 00:44:27,856
Smiley face.

1046
00:44:30,586 --> 00:44:31,656
Thank you.

1047
00:44:34,126 --> 00:44:36,026
What is it?

1048
00:44:36,126 --> 00:44:37,366
(Have they changed since they first met?)

1049
00:44:37,366 --> 00:44:39,566
So this is how it feels. We shouldn't have read that.

1050
00:44:39,566 --> 00:44:40,596
Why?

1051
00:44:44,206 --> 00:44:46,576
(Min Young is back from the date.)

1052
00:44:46,576 --> 00:44:47,576
What?

1053
00:44:47,876 --> 00:44:49,036
I'm...

1054
00:44:49,676 --> 00:44:51,746
- I'm not feeling so well...
- Are you feeling sick?

1055
00:44:51,746 --> 00:44:54,676
I think I'm losing my voice.

1056
00:44:54,776 --> 00:44:56,116
- It's starting to go.
- Or...

1057
00:44:56,116 --> 00:44:57,186
Right?

1058
00:44:57,346 --> 00:44:58,486
Drink some ginger latte.

1059
00:44:58,686 --> 00:44:59,986
There's a ginger latte?

1060
00:45:00,256 --> 00:45:01,316
I'll make it for you.

1061
00:45:02,386 --> 00:45:03,386
It's good.

1062
00:45:03,386 --> 00:45:04,756
- Really?
- I love ginger latte.

1063
00:45:05,026 --> 00:45:07,296
Big sis will make you a cup of ginger latte!

1064
00:45:09,256 --> 00:45:12,766
(Big sis is off.)

1065
00:45:13,236 --> 00:45:14,496
Hi.

1066
00:45:15,136 --> 00:45:16,466
Hi.

1067
00:45:17,836 --> 00:45:20,306
(Just then, she runs into Do Gon.)

1068
00:45:20,606 --> 00:45:22,906
- You see, it seems like...
- Yes?

1069
00:45:22,906 --> 00:45:24,806
Ro Bin's cold got worse.

1070
00:45:25,206 --> 00:45:26,206
All of a sudden?

1071
00:45:26,776 --> 00:45:28,716
Did she already have a bit of a cold?

1072
00:45:28,846 --> 00:45:29,886
- I'm not sure.
- Ro Bin might've said...

1073
00:45:29,886 --> 00:45:31,186
she had a sore throat.

1074
00:45:31,186 --> 00:45:33,516
But she looks quite sick right now.

1075
00:45:34,016 --> 00:45:35,016
Oh, dear.

1076
00:45:36,386 --> 00:45:38,986
I was going to make ginger latte, but we don't have ginger tea.

1077
00:45:40,496 --> 00:45:41,656
There's no lemon marmalade either.

1078
00:45:41,656 --> 00:45:43,166
(Worried)

1079
00:45:44,226 --> 00:45:45,226
We don't have any, do we?

1080
00:45:45,596 --> 00:45:48,766
I've asked for it.

1081
00:45:48,766 --> 00:45:50,166
- We don't have ginger tea.
- Fever...

1082
00:45:50,566 --> 00:45:52,506
- Is that so?
- Do you drink citrus tea?

1083
00:45:52,506 --> 00:45:53,606
I do, and I like citrus tea.

1084
00:45:53,606 --> 00:45:55,176
- Do you drink citrus chamomile tea?
- She already made one.

1085
00:45:55,176 --> 00:45:56,546
Yes, of course.

1086
00:45:56,546 --> 00:45:58,506
- It's citrus chamomile tea.
- Thank you.

1087
00:45:58,506 --> 00:45:59,746
Drink it even if it's bad.

1088
00:45:59,746 --> 00:46:01,746
No, I'll drink it. I'll definitely drink it all.

1089
00:46:01,746 --> 00:46:03,846
- Do you have a fever?
- What?

1090
00:46:03,946 --> 00:46:05,416
No, I don't think so.

1091
00:46:05,516 --> 00:46:07,616
- Should I take my temperature?
- You're like a doctor.

1092
00:46:07,616 --> 00:46:09,286
- Really?
- I brought one.

1093
00:46:09,286 --> 00:46:10,386
What's this? How do you use it?

1094
00:46:10,386 --> 00:46:11,426
Get ready.

1095
00:46:12,186 --> 00:46:13,196
Your voice sounds a little weird.

1096
00:46:13,196 --> 00:46:14,656
Yes, I've kind of lost it.

1097
00:46:14,826 --> 00:46:16,026
- Fever...
- You don't have a fever.

1098
00:46:16,026 --> 00:46:17,596
Right? I don't feel like I do.

1099
00:46:17,696 --> 00:46:19,096
(Do Gon takes Ro Bin's temperature himself.)

1100
00:46:19,096 --> 00:46:20,196
No, you don't have a fever.

1101
00:46:20,336 --> 00:46:22,266
I did go to the hospital and get some medicine.

1102
00:46:22,266 --> 00:46:25,536
- Today?
- I was told not to talk much,

1103
00:46:25,536 --> 00:46:26,576
but I talked a lot.

1104
00:46:26,876 --> 00:46:28,606
- So you shouldn't talk much.
- No.

1105
00:46:28,606 --> 00:46:31,106
It's okay to talk in a small voice.

1106
00:46:31,646 --> 00:46:33,946
Get some rest while you drink that.

1107
00:46:33,946 --> 00:46:35,916
Okay, thank you.

1108
00:46:36,586 --> 00:46:39,116
(Teasing)

1109
00:46:41,186 --> 00:46:42,516
(Feeling shy)

1110
00:46:43,186 --> 00:46:44,986
I told him on purpose.

1111
00:46:44,986 --> 00:46:46,456
Ro Bin is sick.

1112
00:46:46,456 --> 00:46:47,796
Well done.

1113
00:46:47,796 --> 00:46:48,796
I...

1114
00:46:49,426 --> 00:46:51,326
I guess I kind of enjoy this. Oh, dear.

1115
00:46:51,326 --> 00:46:52,466
(Cupid Min Young works her magic.)

1116
00:46:52,466 --> 00:46:53,466
It was fun.

1117
00:46:54,166 --> 00:46:57,306
(1 hour later)

1118
00:47:00,036 --> 00:47:04,846
(Do Gon returns with something he bought outside.)

1119
00:47:05,376 --> 00:47:06,376
Wait.

1120
00:47:07,046 --> 00:47:08,046
Yes?

1121
00:47:08,816 --> 00:47:10,146
Yes? What is it?

1122
00:47:10,516 --> 00:47:11,516
Do you feel better?

1123
00:47:11,616 --> 00:47:13,586
- No, I'm still...
- Here's some medicinal herb tea.

1124
00:47:14,156 --> 00:47:15,356
Thank you.

1125
00:47:15,356 --> 00:47:16,456
Jujube medicinal herb tea.

1126
00:47:16,656 --> 00:47:19,456
- Drink one right now.
- Okay.

1127
00:47:19,456 --> 00:47:22,696
The rest... You can just leave these here.

1128
00:47:22,896 --> 00:47:23,926
What's this?

1129
00:47:24,126 --> 00:47:25,696
- Ginger tea.
- Ginger tea.

1130
00:47:26,126 --> 00:47:27,866
- You need hot water for this.
- Right.

1131
00:47:28,296 --> 00:47:29,906
- I'll leave this downstairs.
- This...

1132
00:47:29,906 --> 00:47:31,536
- Are you taking this downstairs?
- It's warm. Yes.

1133
00:47:31,636 --> 00:47:32,706
- I...
- No, I'll do it.

1134
00:47:33,306 --> 00:47:34,476
Thank you.

1135
00:47:35,536 --> 00:47:36,546
I'd better drink it.

1136
00:47:36,546 --> 00:47:37,906
- Right now?
- Right now.

1137
00:47:37,906 --> 00:47:40,046
It's warm. I appreciate it.

1138
00:47:40,416 --> 00:47:42,276
- Being sick is a no-no.
- Exactly.

1139
00:47:42,816 --> 00:47:44,616
- As expected.
- Did you see that?

1140
00:47:44,616 --> 00:47:46,586
- I knew he'd do that.
- Gosh, Do Gon.

1141
00:47:46,586 --> 00:47:48,756
Today's ginger tea timing was nice.

1142
00:47:48,856 --> 00:47:51,026
- It was very nice.
- Yes, very nice.

1143
00:47:51,026 --> 00:47:52,756
- Very nice - Nice

1144
00:47:54,656 --> 00:47:56,596
- He's always so cool.
- Do Gon is the best.

1145
00:47:56,596 --> 00:47:58,796
I feel at ease when Do Gon appears.

1146
00:47:58,796 --> 00:48:00,766
- Right?
- I feel at ease.

1147
00:48:00,996 --> 00:48:02,136
He just hits the spot.

1148
00:48:02,436 --> 00:48:03,836
When someone takes care of you when you're sick,

1149
00:48:03,836 --> 00:48:04,836
you can't help but catch feelings.

1150
00:48:04,836 --> 00:48:06,506
- Absolutely.
- How is he that sweet?

1151
00:48:07,706 --> 00:48:11,476
(In the bottles are Do Gon's feelings.)

1152
00:48:17,680 --> 00:48:20,780
(Ye Ji and Ro Bin are the only ones in the girls' room.)

1153
00:48:20,780 --> 00:48:23,020
Really, Ye Ji.

1154
00:48:24,950 --> 00:48:27,360
I've never dated before.

1155
00:48:28,520 --> 00:48:30,430
It's only natural for it to be tough, right?

1156
00:48:30,430 --> 00:48:31,460
Totally.

1157
00:48:31,460 --> 00:48:34,500
Was your first relationship also a little tough?

1158
00:48:34,500 --> 00:48:36,800
Of course. It was really tough.

1159
00:48:37,200 --> 00:48:39,300
I keep... You know...

1160
00:48:40,140 --> 00:48:43,110
I keep thinking, "Can I start a conversation?"

1161
00:48:43,510 --> 00:48:45,410
You know, things like that?

1162
00:48:45,410 --> 00:48:46,710
There's a need for us to be...

1163
00:48:46,710 --> 00:48:47,710
- more proactive.
- Is that so?

1164
00:48:48,210 --> 00:48:50,350
It's already Day Four.

1165
00:48:50,880 --> 00:48:52,250
Tomorrow will be Day Five.

1166
00:48:53,280 --> 00:48:54,650
There are only two days left.

1167
00:48:54,650 --> 00:48:57,120
Exactly. We're short on time.

1168
00:48:57,120 --> 00:48:58,150
True.

1169
00:48:58,420 --> 00:49:02,020
Even if we act with more enthusiasm...

1170
00:49:02,420 --> 00:49:04,860
It's definitely easier said than done.

1171
00:49:06,130 --> 00:49:07,460
Bon appetit.

1172
00:49:07,460 --> 00:49:09,160
- Good job.
- Thank you for the meal.

1173
00:49:09,630 --> 00:49:10,870
Let's dig in, or it'll get cold.

1174
00:49:12,730 --> 00:49:14,800
- Whose rice is this?
- Mine.

1175
00:49:14,800 --> 00:49:16,670
Is that so? Then I'll put mine here.

1176
00:49:16,670 --> 00:49:17,770
(Each takes a seat.)

1177
00:49:17,770 --> 00:49:18,770
After dinner...

1178
00:49:20,410 --> 00:49:21,480
(The 2 sit 1 seat away from each other.)

1179
00:49:21,480 --> 00:49:22,480
Don't we have six people?

1180
00:49:22,480 --> 00:49:23,510
- Hold on. 1, 2...
- Would you like this seat?

1181
00:49:23,510 --> 00:49:24,550
(The 2 sit 1 seat away from each other.)

1182
00:49:24,550 --> 00:49:26,450
- Will you be sitting there, Ye Ji?
- No.

1183
00:49:26,450 --> 00:49:28,320
- Would you like this seat?
- I'm feeling a bit hot.

1184
00:49:28,320 --> 00:49:30,190
- May I turn the AC on?
- Sure.

1185
00:49:30,390 --> 00:49:32,220
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1186
00:49:32,220 --> 00:49:34,390
- Seon Ho is left-handed, - Really?

1187
00:49:34,390 --> 00:49:35,860
- so he'll probably sit at the end.
- Is that so?

1188
00:49:35,860 --> 00:49:37,360
I didn't know he was left-handed.

1189
00:49:37,360 --> 00:49:39,290
- Is this yours?
- Yes.

1190
00:49:39,290 --> 00:49:42,630
(Leaving the end seat for left-handed Seon Ho)

1191
00:49:42,830 --> 00:49:44,270
- Someone is looking for you.
- Right?

1192
00:49:44,270 --> 00:49:49,440
(Seon Ho has been sitting in the same seat since the first day.)

1193
00:49:50,070 --> 00:49:51,940
(Last night's dinner)

1194
00:49:51,940 --> 00:49:53,640
- Can I really sit here?
- Yes.

1195
00:49:53,740 --> 00:49:55,240
- I'm left-handed.
- Is that so?

1196
00:49:55,240 --> 00:49:57,780
That's why I always take the end seat.

1197
00:50:01,080 --> 00:50:02,280
So this is what it's like.

1198
00:50:03,550 --> 00:50:04,920
It's pretty.

1199
00:50:04,920 --> 00:50:08,390
(Seon Ho's designated seat next to Ro Bin is left empty.)

1200
00:50:15,330 --> 00:50:16,370
Right?

1201
00:50:16,370 --> 00:50:17,970
Should I leave this in the center?

1202
00:50:19,500 --> 00:50:20,840
(Pulling)

1203
00:50:21,370 --> 00:50:22,670
- What?
- For real?

1204
00:50:23,270 --> 00:50:24,870
- What?
- What's going on?

1205
00:50:26,010 --> 00:50:27,440
(Pulling)

1206
00:50:27,610 --> 00:50:28,680
Is this all?

1207
00:50:29,440 --> 00:50:30,450
- What?
- What is it?

1208
00:50:30,850 --> 00:50:33,520
- Min Young...
- Min Young?

1209
00:50:33,520 --> 00:50:34,650
Can I?

1210
00:50:34,750 --> 00:50:35,780
She went to talk.

1211
00:50:35,780 --> 00:50:39,190
(Seon Ho abandoned his designated seat and sat next to Ye Ji.)

1212
00:50:43,830 --> 00:50:46,190
(This is what we're talking about!)

1213
00:50:46,190 --> 00:50:47,700
Congratulations.

1214
00:50:47,900 --> 00:50:49,460
(Impressed)

1215
00:50:49,460 --> 00:50:50,700
This is hip-hop.

1216
00:50:50,800 --> 00:50:51,800
He killed it.

1217
00:50:52,870 --> 00:50:53,900
Thank you.

1218
00:50:53,900 --> 00:50:55,540
- Thank you very much.
- Goodness, Seon Ho!

1219
00:50:55,540 --> 00:50:56,910
He has us twisted around his finger.

1220
00:50:56,910 --> 00:50:57,910
For real.

1221
00:50:57,910 --> 00:50:59,070
Seon Ho has changed.

1222
00:50:59,740 --> 00:51:01,580
For Seon Ho to have gone that far...

1223
00:51:02,080 --> 00:51:04,710
means he's tried hard.

1224
00:51:04,710 --> 00:51:06,050
- Totally.
- He put in full effort.

1225
00:51:06,050 --> 00:51:08,280
- After the game, - Yes?

1226
00:51:08,550 --> 00:51:09,550
they sort of checked...

1227
00:51:09,550 --> 00:51:10,950
- each other's feelings.
- Right.

1228
00:51:10,950 --> 00:51:13,790
It feels like Seon Ho has decided to go...

1229
00:51:13,790 --> 00:51:15,520
- straight for her.
- Did he?

1230
00:51:15,520 --> 00:51:16,790
Ye Ji's right arm...

1231
00:51:16,890 --> 00:51:18,960
and Seon Ho's left arm will touch.

1232
00:51:19,760 --> 00:51:21,600
- That's correct.
- He wants to reach her.

1233
00:51:21,600 --> 00:51:23,700
Yes, he wants their arms to touch.

1234
00:51:23,700 --> 00:51:25,300
That's insane.

1235
00:51:28,800 --> 00:51:30,070
- What's this?
- Is there no sauce for this?

1236
00:51:30,070 --> 00:51:31,110
Did you try it?

1237
00:51:31,110 --> 00:51:32,510
- Over here?
- The ketchup.

1238
00:51:32,610 --> 00:51:33,980
It was really good.

1239
00:51:34,480 --> 00:51:36,380
- I can't imagine it.
- The orange was...

1240
00:51:37,210 --> 00:51:42,320
(Enduring the discomfort, Seon Ho secured the seat next to Ye Ji's.)

1241
00:51:43,150 --> 00:51:45,320
Having meat after vegan food is a bit...

1242
00:51:46,320 --> 00:51:50,260
(Do Gon brings up the date he had with Ye Ji.)

1243
00:51:54,060 --> 00:51:56,360
- It didn't taste vegan at all.
- Right?

1244
00:51:57,800 --> 00:52:00,000
What was the name again? Orange something.

1245
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:02,140
It was deep-fried something.

1246
00:52:03,040 --> 00:52:05,240
- I'm getting curious.
- Orange onion?

1247
00:52:05,340 --> 00:52:06,740
It was really good.

1248
00:52:07,140 --> 00:52:09,810
- I can't imagine it.
- The orange was deep-fried.

1249
00:52:10,150 --> 00:52:11,810
It felt like eating fried chicken.

1250
00:52:12,480 --> 00:52:15,450
The restaurant deep-fried oranges.

1251
00:52:16,280 --> 00:52:17,350
That's how it felt.

1252
00:52:17,850 --> 00:52:19,120
Either way, the food was good.

1253
00:52:22,760 --> 00:52:25,030
I was conscious of Do Gon.

1254
00:52:25,460 --> 00:52:28,230
I felt frustrated, as if I were being chased by something.

1255
00:52:28,460 --> 00:52:30,070
Be wishy-washy,

1256
00:52:30,600 --> 00:52:33,770
and things might just end nowhere.

1257
00:52:35,200 --> 00:52:40,080
(For the first time, Seon Ho has grown impatient.)

1258
00:52:41,440 --> 00:52:44,250
(After dinner)

1259
00:52:46,310 --> 00:52:47,520
(Screaming)

1260
00:52:47,520 --> 00:52:48,520
What's wrong?

1261
00:52:49,550 --> 00:52:50,550
Did you get hurt?

1262
00:52:51,220 --> 00:52:53,720
My nail broke. Right here.

1263
00:52:53,990 --> 00:52:55,560
- Does it hurt?
- Yes.

1264
00:52:56,590 --> 00:52:58,630
What should we do? How did it happen?

1265
00:52:58,630 --> 00:53:01,960
- My nail was already kind of loose.
- I see.

1266
00:53:02,660 --> 00:53:03,670
Give me a second.

1267
00:53:06,100 --> 00:53:09,870
(Seon Ho heads somewhere.)

1268
00:53:13,780 --> 00:53:15,740
(Looking around)

1269
00:53:18,250 --> 00:53:20,950
(Found the first-aid kit)

1270
00:53:21,920 --> 00:53:23,290
- Oh, my gosh.
- It's over here.

1271
00:53:23,850 --> 00:53:24,850
Here.

1272
00:53:24,850 --> 00:53:27,060
(Just in time, Ye Ji came for some medicine.)

1273
00:53:28,460 --> 00:53:30,290
Put this on, and don't use your hand.

1274
00:53:33,260 --> 00:53:34,500
Here, show me.

1275
00:53:37,900 --> 00:53:39,070
Is this where...

1276
00:53:39,670 --> 00:53:40,800
Should we apply it here?

1277
00:53:43,740 --> 00:53:47,480
(Being thorough)

1278
00:53:49,380 --> 00:53:50,410
I'll do it.

1279
00:53:51,450 --> 00:53:53,180
I'll do it. Stay still.

1280
00:53:55,580 --> 00:53:57,550
(Laughing)

1281
00:53:58,690 --> 00:53:59,690
Like so.

1282
00:53:59,850 --> 00:54:00,920
(Lightly)

1283
00:54:00,920 --> 00:54:03,660
- Is it waterproof?
- Yes, it's like rubber gloves.

1284
00:54:08,460 --> 00:54:13,200
(The moment when his feelings are conveyed through her fingertip)

1285
00:54:13,770 --> 00:54:16,610
This is tough to roll down.

1286
00:54:16,840 --> 00:54:17,970
I think he's done,

1287
00:54:17,970 --> 00:54:19,210
- but he keeps touching her.
- Right?

1288
00:54:19,210 --> 00:54:21,410
- He was done a long time ago.
- Totally.

1289
00:54:21,410 --> 00:54:22,880
You might as well put a cast on.

1290
00:54:24,880 --> 00:54:26,410
That's practically a cast.

1291
00:54:26,820 --> 00:54:28,780
Aren't we all set? We've seen it all.

1292
00:54:28,780 --> 00:54:30,090
We already have one couple.

1293
00:54:30,090 --> 00:54:31,820
- Yes, congratulations.
- For real.

1294
00:54:31,820 --> 00:54:32,920
Congratulations, Seon Ho and Ye Ji.

1295
00:54:32,920 --> 00:54:34,590
- It's certain.
- He's back.

1296
00:54:34,590 --> 00:54:35,590
But guys.

1297
00:54:35,960 --> 00:54:36,960
(You never know.)

1298
00:54:36,960 --> 00:54:39,160
- Don't do that.
- Stop spoiling it.

1299
00:54:39,160 --> 00:54:40,860
- No.
- Guys.

1300
00:54:40,860 --> 00:54:41,860
- Stop it.
- Don't.

1301
00:54:41,860 --> 00:54:42,930
- Can things get twisted here?
- Guys.

1302
00:54:42,930 --> 00:54:43,970
Things are going completely fine.

1303
00:54:43,970 --> 00:54:45,170
The two are set in stone.

1304
00:54:45,170 --> 00:54:47,740
- How can things go wrong?
- We're being rash.

1305
00:54:47,740 --> 00:54:49,470
I want to be rash.

1306
00:54:49,470 --> 00:54:50,940
I want to be rash too.

1307
00:54:51,370 --> 00:54:53,140
Don't take Love Against Time for granted.

1308
00:54:55,180 --> 00:54:56,180
What a golden saying.

1309
00:54:56,180 --> 00:54:59,210
Right? Don't take Love Against Time for granted.

1310
00:54:59,710 --> 00:55:02,420
Seon Ho is expressing his feelings to me.

1311
00:55:02,420 --> 00:55:03,720
That was what crossed my mind.

1312
00:55:03,720 --> 00:55:05,090
I was very grateful.

1313
00:55:05,420 --> 00:55:08,620
My heart also fluttered. It made me happy.

1314
00:55:10,160 --> 00:55:12,630
Just in case, take a few...

1315
00:55:12,630 --> 00:55:14,060
- Okay.
- Band-Aids.

1316
00:55:14,560 --> 00:55:15,830
- Thank you.
- No problem.

1317
00:55:16,970 --> 00:55:18,300
This much should do.

1318
00:55:19,700 --> 00:55:21,200
Thanks for driving.

1319
00:55:21,200 --> 00:55:22,900
Don't worry about it. Good job today.

1320
00:55:22,900 --> 00:55:24,140
Good job to you as well.

1321
00:55:24,140 --> 00:55:25,440
You found it yourself.

1322
00:55:25,440 --> 00:55:26,440
True.

1323
00:55:28,740 --> 00:55:30,450
(Sighing)

1324
00:55:32,650 --> 00:55:35,080
Do Gon, did you have a productive conversation?

1325
00:55:35,650 --> 00:55:36,690
I did.

1326
00:55:39,190 --> 00:55:42,120
The time gave me a chance to sort things out...

1327
00:55:42,520 --> 00:55:43,860
- Really?
- for myself.

1328
00:55:44,430 --> 00:55:46,260
Did it go well?

1329
00:55:46,630 --> 00:55:48,700
I decided to go back...

1330
00:55:48,700 --> 00:55:49,730
- to how I was...
- Right.

1331
00:55:49,730 --> 00:55:50,930
in the beginning.

1332
00:55:52,870 --> 00:55:54,670
And you, Jong Eun?

1333
00:55:54,670 --> 00:55:56,100
- I plan...
- Did you make progress?

1334
00:55:56,500 --> 00:55:58,340
to be like you.

1335
00:55:59,040 --> 00:56:01,410
You know...

1336
00:56:01,410 --> 00:56:03,240
There's no other way, is there?

1337
00:56:04,310 --> 00:56:07,180
- Leave no regrets.
- Go for it.

1338
00:56:07,180 --> 00:56:08,520
No looking back.

1339
00:56:11,590 --> 00:56:13,290
- Isn't that better?
- Yes.

1340
00:56:19,408 --> 00:56:24,048
(The four have come out for some fresh air in the nice weather.)

1341
00:56:25,048 --> 00:56:26,118
It's nice.

1342
00:56:26,118 --> 00:56:27,118
It sure is.

1343
00:56:27,118 --> 00:56:29,958
But it could suddenly become cold.

1344
00:56:29,958 --> 00:56:31,788
Gosh, the moon looks pretty.

1345
00:56:33,328 --> 00:56:35,658
(The moon is particularly bright today.)

1346
00:56:36,228 --> 00:56:39,158
(The moonlight softly illuminates the city at night.)

1347
00:56:44,168 --> 00:56:45,498
(Settling in at the end of the terrace,)

1348
00:56:45,498 --> 00:56:48,038
(where the moon is clearly visible)

1349
00:56:50,578 --> 00:56:57,518
(Jong Eun stares quietly at the moon, as if deep in thought.)

1350
00:57:01,618 --> 00:57:03,618
Where did Jong Eun go?

1351
00:57:03,618 --> 00:57:04,618
- He's at the very end.
- Over...

1352
00:57:04,618 --> 00:57:05,958
Is he over there alone?

1353
00:57:08,628 --> 00:57:10,898
He's enjoying some solitude.

1354
00:57:11,398 --> 00:57:13,498
The moon looks...

1355
00:57:13,498 --> 00:57:15,668
particularly big from over there.

1356
00:57:16,528 --> 00:57:18,298
- Isn't the moon pretty?
- It's pretty.

1357
00:57:18,838 --> 00:57:19,938
Do you want to go there?

1358
00:57:19,938 --> 00:57:21,568
We might be able to see it better.

1359
00:57:21,568 --> 00:57:23,478
- Where?
- Should we go over to that side?

1360
00:57:24,708 --> 00:57:25,708
Come over here.

1361
00:57:25,708 --> 00:57:27,408
(Ro Bin walks over to Jong Eun, using the moon as an excuse.)

1362
00:57:27,408 --> 00:57:30,118
Doesn't the cold air make you feel like you're about to cough?

1363
00:57:31,248 --> 00:57:32,978
- Jong Eun, what are you doing?
- What are you doing?

1364
00:57:33,118 --> 00:57:34,348
- What?
- Are you lost in thought?

1365
00:57:34,348 --> 00:57:35,988
No, I was enjoying the night view.

1366
00:57:36,218 --> 00:57:37,458
You were?

1367
00:57:37,458 --> 00:57:38,518
Yes.

1368
00:57:40,488 --> 00:57:42,688
Jong Eun, have you thought of your wish?

1369
00:57:42,688 --> 00:57:44,098
- Me?
- You forgot, didn't you?

1370
00:57:44,498 --> 00:57:45,558
Well, no.

1371
00:57:45,558 --> 00:57:46,558
Did you forget about it?

1372
00:57:46,558 --> 00:57:48,028
No, I've been thinking about it.

1373
00:57:48,028 --> 00:57:49,028
You forgot, right?

1374
00:57:49,028 --> 00:57:50,738
No, I didn't. I've really been thinking...

1375
00:57:50,738 --> 00:57:51,798
But you did... Really?

1376
00:57:51,798 --> 00:57:53,198
Have you been thinking about it?

1377
00:57:53,638 --> 00:57:54,638
I see.

1378
00:57:54,638 --> 00:57:55,808
Today was hectic,

1379
00:57:55,808 --> 00:57:57,138
- having to go to the hospital.
- Right?

1380
00:57:57,138 --> 00:57:58,438
What did the result say?

1381
00:57:58,938 --> 00:58:00,208
- It turned out fine.
- Did it?

1382
00:58:00,208 --> 00:58:01,548
What did the blood test say?

1383
00:58:01,548 --> 00:58:03,918
My platelet count was a little high,

1384
00:58:03,918 --> 00:58:06,048
but the doctor said it was still okay.

1385
00:58:07,048 --> 00:58:08,918
Does your mouth still feel dry?

1386
00:58:09,388 --> 00:58:13,088
Yes, but I think time will take care of it.

1387
00:58:14,428 --> 00:58:17,658
You don't know when it'll get better, do you?

1388
00:58:18,828 --> 00:58:20,068
- It...
- It'll last forever.

1389
00:58:20,068 --> 00:58:21,068
Forever?

1390
00:58:21,068 --> 00:58:22,798
- Yes.
- How come?

1391
00:58:22,798 --> 00:58:24,398
It could last forever or not.

1392
00:58:24,398 --> 00:58:25,668
It's a complete gamble...

1393
00:58:25,668 --> 00:58:28,368
since everyone is different.

1394
00:58:28,368 --> 00:58:31,138
I believe 100 percent that you'll get better.

1395
00:58:31,138 --> 00:58:32,138
- Really?
- Yes.

1396
00:58:32,138 --> 00:58:33,238
How come?

1397
00:58:33,378 --> 00:58:34,408
What?

1398
00:58:34,408 --> 00:58:35,808
I'm just...

1399
00:58:35,808 --> 00:58:36,818
Even when I'm sick,

1400
00:58:36,818 --> 00:58:39,878
I never think of the worst.

1401
00:58:41,318 --> 00:58:43,188
Why do you think it'll last forever...

1402
00:58:43,188 --> 00:58:45,718
- and not get better?
- What?

1403
00:58:45,718 --> 00:58:47,788
Why do you think it won't get better?

1404
00:58:47,788 --> 00:58:51,028
- I do think it'll get better.
- I see.

1405
00:58:51,528 --> 00:58:53,768
- But?
- But this is lifelong homework.

1406
00:58:55,228 --> 00:58:57,698
You worry too much, don't you?

1407
00:58:57,698 --> 00:58:58,998
- Me?
- Yes.

1408
00:58:58,998 --> 00:59:00,168
- I'm not worried.
- You're not?

1409
00:59:00,168 --> 00:59:01,968
- I do worry, - Yes?

1410
00:59:01,968 --> 00:59:04,178
- but not too deeply.
- Right.

1411
00:59:04,178 --> 00:59:05,378
It's just...

1412
00:59:05,908 --> 00:59:09,478
I just don't know what to do.

1413
00:59:10,148 --> 00:59:11,178
It's tough.

1414
00:59:11,178 --> 00:59:12,448
- Is it?
- Yes.

1415
00:59:15,348 --> 00:59:17,218
- Have you talked...
- Yes?

1416
00:59:17,218 --> 00:59:18,888
with the others a lot?

1417
00:59:20,188 --> 00:59:22,128
Honestly, I just...

1418
00:59:22,128 --> 00:59:24,258
Who have you talked with the most?

1419
00:59:26,298 --> 00:59:28,868
- It's probably you, Ro Bin.
- Seriously?

1420
00:59:29,498 --> 00:59:30,798
Like having actual conversations.

1421
00:59:30,798 --> 00:59:31,968
Is that so?

1422
00:59:32,838 --> 00:59:34,238
I see.

1423
00:59:37,678 --> 00:59:38,838
You know, I...

1424
00:59:40,448 --> 00:59:42,608
Expressing...

1425
00:59:43,718 --> 00:59:45,648
my feelings first...

1426
00:59:45,648 --> 00:59:49,248
and doing things like that are both a first for me.

1427
00:59:49,248 --> 00:59:50,258
- Is that so?
- Yes.

1428
00:59:50,258 --> 00:59:52,518
I've never done it before in my life.

1429
00:59:52,518 --> 00:59:54,328
So I don't know how to do it.

1430
00:59:54,328 --> 00:59:56,388
I'm really bad at it.

1431
00:59:56,388 --> 00:59:57,598
I don't even know...

1432
00:59:57,598 --> 00:59:59,128
- if I'm on the right track.
- Me too.

1433
01:00:00,768 --> 01:00:03,798
(Laughing)

1434
01:00:03,798 --> 01:00:06,368
I've been wanting to know what kind of talks...

1435
01:00:06,368 --> 01:00:08,168
- we should have.
- That's natural.

1436
01:00:08,168 --> 01:00:11,738
I was able to talk to many people,

1437
01:00:11,738 --> 01:00:14,578
and I talked to them a lot in the earlier days.

1438
01:00:14,578 --> 01:00:15,648
- Really?
- Yes.

1439
01:00:15,648 --> 01:00:16,948
What's the conclusion you came to?

1440
01:00:17,618 --> 01:00:19,378
There are some...

1441
01:00:19,378 --> 01:00:23,088
who have expressed their interest in me.

1442
01:00:25,388 --> 01:00:28,428
But I have someone in mind.

1443
01:00:28,428 --> 01:00:30,898
Among the people you're interested in?

1444
01:00:30,898 --> 01:00:34,268
No, not among the people.

1445
01:00:34,268 --> 01:00:37,468
I've settled on someone.

1446
01:00:38,368 --> 01:00:39,438
That's right.

1447
01:00:40,838 --> 01:00:43,978
You're too slow.

1448
01:00:43,978 --> 01:00:46,508
Hurry up and talk to others.

1449
01:00:46,508 --> 01:00:49,378
Spend the rest of your time investing in that one person.

1450
01:00:51,248 --> 01:00:54,948
But there's someone I'd like to get to know.

1451
01:00:57,588 --> 01:00:58,718
I see.

1452
01:01:01,988 --> 01:01:03,128
Right.

1453
01:01:07,368 --> 01:01:09,368
They can't reach each other.

1454
01:01:09,368 --> 01:01:12,198
- Jong Eun is super closed off.
- Right?

1455
01:01:12,198 --> 01:01:14,068
- This is a tough one.
- True.

1456
01:01:15,438 --> 01:01:18,538
But we know how he feels.

1457
01:01:19,138 --> 01:01:20,878
You can't do anything about it.

1458
01:01:20,878 --> 01:01:22,348
- For sure.
- You're right.

1459
01:01:24,178 --> 01:01:25,178
Aren't you cold?

1460
01:01:25,178 --> 01:01:27,318
- No, I'm not.
- Is that so?

1461
01:01:27,318 --> 01:01:30,048
I'm totally fine right now.

1462
01:01:30,048 --> 01:01:32,388
I want to keep this conversation going,

1463
01:01:32,388 --> 01:01:34,428
but do you want to as well?

1464
01:01:34,888 --> 01:01:36,658
- Me? With you?
- Yes.

1465
01:01:37,928 --> 01:01:38,958
Well...

1466
01:01:38,958 --> 01:01:43,168
I'm willing to talk to you...

1467
01:01:44,438 --> 01:01:45,698
until...

1468
01:01:46,638 --> 01:01:47,638
you want to.

1469
01:01:47,638 --> 01:01:49,568
But I have someone...

1470
01:01:49,568 --> 01:01:51,108
- Of course.
- I'd like to get to know.

1471
01:01:51,108 --> 01:01:54,348
I want you to talk to her as much as possible.

1472
01:01:54,348 --> 01:01:55,648
- I see.
- Yes.

1473
01:01:55,648 --> 01:01:59,248
I want you to have as many conversations as possible. I...

1474
01:01:59,818 --> 01:02:02,018
There's really not enough time.

1475
01:02:04,788 --> 01:02:07,828
I didn't know what to say. I was at a loss for words.

1476
01:02:08,228 --> 01:02:10,498
It was upsetting.

1477
01:02:11,128 --> 01:02:13,498
No matter what I said,

1478
01:02:13,498 --> 01:02:15,898
it felt like it bounced off of him.

1479
01:02:16,938 --> 01:02:18,098
Then...

1480
01:02:19,398 --> 01:02:22,968
Think about your wish and tell me.

1481
01:02:22,968 --> 01:02:24,338
Got it.

1482
01:02:24,778 --> 01:02:26,178
Think about it, okay?

1483
01:02:31,348 --> 01:02:38,918
(Do Gon can hear Ro Bin and Jong Eun's conversation.)

1484
01:02:40,988 --> 01:02:42,658
- Was he listening to them?
- Oh, no.

1485
01:02:42,658 --> 01:02:43,728
- For real?
- The camera angle.

1486
01:02:43,728 --> 01:02:45,758
- What's with the angle?
- My gosh.

1487
01:02:45,758 --> 01:02:47,098
Was he listening to them just now?

1488
01:02:47,268 --> 01:02:48,898
- Gosh.
- Seriously.

1489
01:02:48,898 --> 01:02:50,028
(Heartbroken)

1490
01:02:50,028 --> 01:02:52,538
- Do Gon is unbelievable.
- Right?

1491
01:02:52,898 --> 01:02:54,038
Yong Hwa.

1492
01:02:54,038 --> 01:02:55,068
My heart hurts.

1493
01:02:55,068 --> 01:02:56,268
It's really...

1494
01:02:56,268 --> 01:02:58,178
My heart is breaking into pieces.

1495
01:02:58,638 --> 01:02:59,938
I'm losing it.

1496
01:03:00,678 --> 01:03:02,408
It hurts.

1497
01:03:06,418 --> 01:03:10,288
(Do Gon forces himself to look away.)

1498
01:03:14,628 --> 01:03:15,628
Did you say you had a younger sister?

1499
01:03:15,958 --> 01:03:17,358
Yes, I did.

1500
01:03:17,358 --> 01:03:18,598
Are you close with her?

1501
01:03:18,928 --> 01:03:20,128
Are you going to stay here?

1502
01:03:20,128 --> 01:03:22,828
Me? Shall we go back inside?

1503
01:03:22,828 --> 01:03:23,998
Well...

1504
01:03:23,998 --> 01:03:25,168
It's already 11pm?

1505
01:03:25,168 --> 01:03:26,598
It's 11pm.

1506
01:03:32,678 --> 01:03:39,018
(Do Gon quietly leaves them alone.)

1507
01:03:40,588 --> 01:03:43,788
Jong Eun and Ro Bin were talking.

1508
01:03:43,788 --> 01:03:46,058
My staying there could've made things...

1509
01:03:46,058 --> 01:03:48,528
awkward for both of them.

1510
01:03:48,528 --> 01:03:50,698
That was why I intentionally left the area.

1511
01:03:53,158 --> 01:03:54,998
(As his feelings for Ro Bin deepen,)

1512
01:03:54,998 --> 01:03:57,838
(he becomes more thoughtful toward her.)

1513
01:03:59,238 --> 01:04:03,508
(Day 4, Do Gon has come to the Room of Time.)

1514
01:04:04,478 --> 01:04:05,478
(The Room of Time Guide)

1515
01:04:05,478 --> 01:04:06,608
(Today, if the total amount of time you allocate to each other...)

1516
01:04:06,608 --> 01:04:07,978
(reaches 110 minutes or more, you'll go on a date.)

1517
01:04:07,978 --> 01:04:09,348
(From this point on,)

1518
01:04:09,348 --> 01:04:10,518
(the total time you've allocated to each other...)

1519
01:04:10,518 --> 01:04:12,448
(will no longer be revealed.)

1520
01:04:12,918 --> 01:04:13,918
What?

1521
01:04:13,918 --> 01:04:16,118
So it's no longer revealed at the end of the date?

1522
01:04:16,548 --> 01:04:17,888
- There's no pressure.
- No.

1523
01:04:17,888 --> 01:04:18,888
There's no pressure.

1524
01:04:18,888 --> 01:04:20,888
The total amount is no longer revealed.

1525
01:04:21,458 --> 01:04:23,228
If so, asking her out on a date is the right thing to do.

1526
01:04:23,228 --> 01:04:24,798
Using up all the time on that person is much better.

1527
01:04:24,798 --> 01:04:26,328
Do Gon would totally think like that.

1528
01:04:26,328 --> 01:04:27,698
There's no pressure if the total amount is...

1529
01:04:27,698 --> 01:04:29,168
- kept a secret.
- Totally.

1530
01:04:31,738 --> 01:04:33,968
When I saw the changed rule...

1531
01:04:33,968 --> 01:04:35,868
Up until yesterday,

1532
01:04:35,868 --> 01:04:37,478
I thought asking her out...

1533
01:04:37,838 --> 01:04:39,878
on a date every time...

1534
01:04:40,308 --> 01:04:44,178
was making her feel uncomfortable.

1535
01:04:44,178 --> 01:04:46,978
That's why I didn't use all my time on her.

1536
01:04:46,978 --> 01:04:49,388
But today,

1537
01:04:49,388 --> 01:04:51,658
the time we allocated to each other...

1538
01:04:51,658 --> 01:04:53,728
won't be revealed.

1539
01:04:54,128 --> 01:04:57,958
"Let's follow my heart." This was the mindset I had.

1540
01:04:58,628 --> 01:05:02,128
The first good feeling I felt...

1541
01:05:02,128 --> 01:05:04,768
hasn't changed.

1542
01:05:06,238 --> 01:05:10,238
(Do Gon's heart couldn't be hidden.)

1543
01:05:10,478 --> 01:05:12,538
It's warm. Thank you.

1544
01:05:13,078 --> 01:05:14,708
- You can't be sick.
- Right.

1545
01:05:17,778 --> 01:05:19,978
(Seo Ro Bin)

1546
01:05:20,988 --> 01:05:25,018
I want to go on a date with her before it's too late.

1547
01:05:25,018 --> 01:05:26,558
I want to talk with her.

1548
01:05:27,688 --> 01:05:29,188
The first thing to do before talking to her...

1549
01:05:30,028 --> 01:05:33,058
was to create that opportunity.

1550
01:05:35,498 --> 01:05:39,598
(Do Gon allocates 100 minutes to Ro Bin.)

1551
01:05:40,538 --> 01:05:43,068
(He uses all of his heart.)

1552
01:05:48,248 --> 01:05:49,248
(Seo Ro Bin)

1553
01:05:49,248 --> 01:05:52,578
(Ro Bin will not know about Do Gon's genuine heart.)

1554
01:05:55,848 --> 01:05:57,288
Hundred Do Gon is back.

1555
01:05:58,358 --> 01:06:01,028
Do Gon is surely the secure type.

1556
01:06:01,088 --> 01:06:02,228
Secure Do Gon.

1557
01:06:02,228 --> 01:06:04,198
If Ro Bin spends ten minutes,

1558
01:06:04,198 --> 01:06:05,498
- the date will happen.
- Right.

1559
01:06:05,498 --> 01:06:06,858
- That will make it 110 minutes.
- Please!

1560
01:06:07,228 --> 01:06:11,238
Ro Bin was slightly pushed back by Jong Eun.

1561
01:06:11,238 --> 01:06:12,368
- Right.
- Right.

1562
01:06:12,368 --> 01:06:13,968
- She was pushed back.
- Right!

1563
01:06:13,968 --> 01:06:16,268
She might not spend 100 minutes...

1564
01:06:16,268 --> 01:06:17,438
- on Jong Eun.
- Right.

1565
01:06:17,708 --> 01:06:19,308
I'm so curious about what she'll do.

1566
01:06:21,948 --> 01:06:24,218
(Ro Bin enters the Room of Time.)

1567
01:06:24,218 --> 01:06:25,278
Let's see.

1568
01:06:29,788 --> 01:06:31,818
I think I've...

1569
01:06:32,488 --> 01:06:36,158
checked his heart to a certain extent.

1570
01:06:36,528 --> 01:06:38,858
He still wants to...

1571
01:06:38,858 --> 01:06:41,728
learn about the others other than me.

1572
01:06:42,128 --> 01:06:44,468
Even still,

1573
01:06:44,468 --> 01:06:48,008
I thought that I should follow my heart.

1574
01:06:48,468 --> 01:06:49,938
(Kim Jong Eun)

1575
01:06:49,938 --> 01:06:52,978
(Ro Bin sends Jong Eun her time...)

1576
01:06:52,978 --> 01:06:55,278
(even though she knows his heart.)

1577
01:06:59,578 --> 01:07:03,858
(Ro Bin allocates 100 minutes to Jong Eun.)

1578
01:07:06,958 --> 01:07:08,828
- Come on!
- Gosh!

1579
01:07:08,828 --> 01:07:11,028
- Everyone's heart is the same.
- Right.

1580
01:07:11,028 --> 01:07:12,158
They all spent 100 minutes?

1581
01:07:12,898 --> 01:07:14,228
- Gosh!
- Ro Bin...

1582
01:07:14,228 --> 01:07:15,768
- is only thinking about Jong Eun.
- She keeps going for Jong Eun.

1583
01:07:16,498 --> 01:07:19,398
- Things are tough.
- Right.

1584
01:07:19,998 --> 01:07:21,668
- That was cold.
- Right.

1585
01:07:27,578 --> 01:07:31,018
(Jong Eun also entered the Room of Time.)

1586
01:07:32,548 --> 01:07:35,648
(His time heads to one name without hesitation.)

1587
01:07:36,448 --> 01:07:38,688
Min Young was always...

1588
01:07:39,118 --> 01:07:41,688
my first priority.

1589
01:07:43,388 --> 01:07:45,798
I wanted to talk with her again.

1590
01:07:46,158 --> 01:07:47,728
That was why I spent 100 minutes on her.

1591
01:07:49,068 --> 01:07:53,398
(Jong Eun allocates 100 minutes to Min Young.)

1592
01:07:53,598 --> 01:07:56,268
If we don't find a connection even after that,

1593
01:07:57,408 --> 01:07:59,538
I think I'll try to turn my eyes to someone else.

1594
01:08:03,348 --> 01:08:06,618
(Where will Min Young's heart head toward?)

1595
01:08:11,018 --> 01:08:12,818
I felt torn about what to do,

1596
01:08:13,188 --> 01:08:14,958
but ever since the moment I came here,

1597
01:08:15,258 --> 01:08:18,458
Seon Ho was the only one who got my attention.

1598
01:08:20,698 --> 01:08:22,798
There was still some time left.

1599
01:08:23,328 --> 01:08:25,798
I thought I could try to approach him a little more.

1600
01:08:26,338 --> 01:08:30,738
"This is how close I can get to him."

1601
01:08:31,238 --> 01:08:33,338
I spent 50 minutes on him with that thought.

1602
01:08:33,338 --> 01:08:35,378
(Min Young allocates 50 minutes to Seon Ho.)

1603
01:08:35,378 --> 01:08:38,248
I've talked a lot with Jong Eun.

1604
01:08:38,248 --> 01:08:39,848
I've talked with Ryun Gi as well.

1605
01:08:39,948 --> 01:08:42,148
Do Gon was the only one I haven't talked with.

1606
01:08:42,688 --> 01:08:46,058
That was why I spent a little bit of my time on him.

1607
01:08:46,058 --> 01:08:47,428
(Han Do Gon)

1608
01:08:47,428 --> 01:08:51,028
(Min Young allocates 30 minutes to Do Gon.)

1609
01:08:52,598 --> 01:08:54,528
I really enjoyed...

1610
01:08:56,098 --> 01:08:57,868
today's date with Ryun Gi.

1611
01:08:58,338 --> 01:09:00,438
I thought I had a great time with him.

1612
01:09:00,868 --> 01:09:02,568
That was why I spent some of time on him as well.

1613
01:09:02,568 --> 01:09:05,278
(Min Young allocates 20 minutes to Ryun Gi.)

1614
01:09:05,938 --> 01:09:10,008
(Min Young's heart doesn't seem to know where to go.)

1615
01:09:12,018 --> 01:09:14,748
It really feels like they are...

1616
01:09:14,888 --> 01:09:16,618
all looking at the back of each other's heads.

1617
01:09:16,618 --> 01:09:18,288
It's pretty much a sports day.

1618
01:09:18,358 --> 01:09:19,358
(A love line that feels like a relay race)

1619
01:09:19,358 --> 01:09:21,088
- A relay race.
- It's a sports day here.

1620
01:09:22,128 --> 01:09:23,858
The baton is passed on to the next person.

1621
01:09:24,698 --> 01:09:26,098
- The running won't stop.
- It's endless.

1622
01:09:26,098 --> 01:09:27,098
- It's endless.
- Gosh!

1623
01:09:27,098 --> 01:09:29,068
When will the running stop?

1624
01:09:29,068 --> 01:09:31,238
- Things are so hard.
- Exactly.

1625
01:09:32,838 --> 01:09:35,908
(The target of Ryun Gi's time)

1626
01:09:37,308 --> 01:09:40,008
It felt like things had just begun for me.

1627
01:09:40,478 --> 01:09:43,178
I thought deeply about who I had to pick.

1628
01:09:45,448 --> 01:09:46,648
During the date with Min Young...

1629
01:09:46,948 --> 01:09:50,418
and Na Young,

1630
01:09:50,658 --> 01:09:54,528
Ro Bin kept lingering inside of my head.

1631
01:09:55,228 --> 01:09:58,028
(After the date of Day 2)

1632
01:09:59,828 --> 01:10:01,828
Without realizing it,

1633
01:10:02,828 --> 01:10:03,998
I think I hurt you.

1634
01:10:05,838 --> 01:10:06,898
I'm sorry.

1635
01:10:08,568 --> 01:10:09,808
It's totally understandable.

1636
01:10:10,338 --> 01:10:13,108
I also worried about the same thing.

1637
01:10:14,408 --> 01:10:16,948
Don't feel bad about it.

1638
01:10:18,648 --> 01:10:22,848
(The conversation with Ro Bin kept bothering him.)

1639
01:10:22,848 --> 01:10:25,488
I want to spend a lot more time...

1640
01:10:27,158 --> 01:10:28,288
with Ro Bin.

1641
01:10:30,958 --> 01:10:32,498
In the Room of Time,

1642
01:10:32,898 --> 01:10:34,998
it felt like I had to go all in with my time.

1643
01:10:40,768 --> 01:10:46,078
(Ryun Gi's time starts heading toward Ro Bin again.)

1644
01:10:50,348 --> 01:10:55,948
(Ryun Gi allocates 100 minutes to Ro Bin.)

1645
01:10:57,958 --> 01:10:59,088
- What?
- Really?

1646
01:10:59,088 --> 01:11:00,888
See? I saw that coming.

1647
01:11:02,358 --> 01:11:03,658
His self-esteem...

1648
01:11:03,658 --> 01:11:05,398
- was brought down by Ro Bin.
- Right.

1649
01:11:05,628 --> 01:11:07,198
But after meeting Na Young...

1650
01:11:07,358 --> 01:11:09,168
- and Min Young, his self-esteem...
- Min Young.

1651
01:11:09,168 --> 01:11:10,428
- went back up.
- He recovered his self-esteem.

1652
01:11:10,428 --> 01:11:12,598
- Right.
- Now,

1653
01:11:12,598 --> 01:11:14,238
- he gained the courage...
- To go forward.

1654
01:11:14,238 --> 01:11:15,368
of being able to do well during dates again.

1655
01:11:15,368 --> 01:11:16,468
- Right.
- Right.

1656
01:11:16,468 --> 01:11:18,008
That's great.

1657
01:11:18,008 --> 01:11:19,338
That's impressive.

1658
01:11:21,508 --> 01:11:24,478
(Ryun Gi meets Ro Bin after making his decision.)

1659
01:11:25,078 --> 01:11:26,318
When are you going to lend me your book?

1660
01:11:26,318 --> 01:11:27,318
Oh, right!

1661
01:11:27,318 --> 01:11:28,688
I was going to...

1662
01:11:29,118 --> 01:11:30,988
read it yesterday.

1663
01:11:31,458 --> 01:11:33,088
But you ran away.

1664
01:11:33,588 --> 01:11:34,588
Right.

1665
01:11:34,588 --> 01:11:35,788
Are you going to give it to me now?

1666
01:11:35,788 --> 01:11:37,228
I'll give it to you now.

1667
01:11:40,058 --> 01:11:41,698
I was reading it.

1668
01:11:41,828 --> 01:11:43,768
- You're lying.
- I'm serious.

1669
01:11:43,768 --> 01:11:44,798
You're lying!

1670
01:11:45,268 --> 01:11:48,008
I was reading it, but I couldn't focus.

1671
01:11:48,208 --> 01:11:49,508
It kept making me fall asleep.

1672
01:11:50,608 --> 01:11:53,808
I should spend some time reading this.

1673
01:11:53,808 --> 01:11:55,978
Right. It's so quiet here.

1674
01:11:56,408 --> 01:11:58,048
Are you busy? Do you have plans for tomorrow?

1675
01:11:58,518 --> 01:11:59,878
- Plans for tomorrow?
- Yes.

1676
01:11:59,878 --> 01:12:01,318
Why do you ask? It's a secret.

1677
01:12:01,688 --> 01:12:02,748
Okay, then.

1678
01:12:03,818 --> 01:12:05,318
I can't do anything about it if it's a secret.

1679
01:12:05,318 --> 01:12:06,458
No. It's not a secret.

1680
01:12:06,758 --> 01:12:10,328
It'll be great to spend time together if you have time.

1681
01:12:11,198 --> 01:12:12,698
Let's go out for a cup of tea.

1682
01:12:12,958 --> 01:12:15,568
Let's hang out. I was going to be bored on my own.

1683
01:12:16,928 --> 01:12:18,468
But why did you say it was a secret?

1684
01:12:18,698 --> 01:12:20,498
- Why hide it?
- I don't know.

1685
01:12:20,498 --> 01:12:22,368
Did you hide it because you felt shy?

1686
01:12:22,468 --> 01:12:23,508
Yes.

1687
01:12:24,838 --> 01:12:28,778
It was so quiet without you today.

1688
01:12:29,278 --> 01:12:30,508
- No way.
- I'm serious.

1689
01:12:30,508 --> 01:12:31,578
What did you do today?

1690
01:12:31,578 --> 01:12:32,948
Who were you with today?

1691
01:12:32,948 --> 01:12:34,748
- Today...
- Weren't you with Seon Ho?

1692
01:12:34,748 --> 01:12:37,618
I was with Seon Ho.

1693
01:12:38,358 --> 01:12:39,988
We talked with each other for a while.

1694
01:12:39,988 --> 01:12:41,188
(Smiling)

1695
01:12:41,188 --> 01:12:42,188
- What is it?
- What?

1696
01:12:42,188 --> 01:12:44,558
- What is it?
- It seems like you're loosening up.

1697
01:12:44,558 --> 01:12:45,658
- Me?
- Yes.

1698
01:12:45,958 --> 01:12:47,028
I feel comfortable.

1699
01:12:47,028 --> 01:12:48,128
- You do?
- Yes.

1700
01:12:48,628 --> 01:12:51,398
You look a lot different from how you looked the first day.

1701
01:12:51,768 --> 01:12:54,308
I feel a lot more comfortable being with you.

1702
01:12:55,108 --> 01:12:56,608
- That's a relief.
- A lot more comfortable.

1703
01:12:56,608 --> 01:12:59,938
That's great for me if you feel that way.

1704
01:13:01,078 --> 01:13:03,608
Seeing you feel anxious...

1705
01:13:03,608 --> 01:13:05,748
made me feel anxious as well.

1706
01:13:05,748 --> 01:13:08,548
- Really?
- Feeling anxious...

1707
01:13:08,548 --> 01:13:10,548
meant that you kept thinking about me.

1708
01:13:10,818 --> 01:13:12,888
But thinking about me in that sense...

1709
01:13:12,888 --> 01:13:14,758
- made me feel anxious as well.
- Right.

1710
01:13:14,758 --> 01:13:17,628
I couldn't expect where that would lead to.

1711
01:13:17,628 --> 01:13:18,628
Right.

1712
01:13:19,028 --> 01:13:20,868
I feel disappointed about that day...

1713
01:13:20,868 --> 01:13:22,128
because...

1714
01:13:22,698 --> 01:13:24,998
I kept freezing...

1715
01:13:24,998 --> 01:13:26,338
and acted awkwardly in front of you.

1716
01:13:26,338 --> 01:13:29,238
I wasn't able to ask you the things I wanted to ask you.

1717
01:13:29,238 --> 01:13:30,538
- Really?
- Yes.

1718
01:13:30,938 --> 01:13:33,708
Because I felt disappointed about that day,

1719
01:13:34,108 --> 01:13:37,178
I wanted to be able to spend more time with you.

1720
01:13:37,448 --> 01:13:39,918
If you have the time,

1721
01:13:40,278 --> 01:13:42,488
I thought we could have a cup of tea together.

1722
01:13:42,788 --> 01:13:44,888
- That sounds good.
- I wanted to be able...

1723
01:13:45,418 --> 01:13:46,418
- to spend time with you.
- I should get...

1724
01:13:46,418 --> 01:13:47,458
a good night's sleep, then.

1725
01:13:47,788 --> 01:13:49,058
Feel comfortable.

1726
01:13:49,058 --> 01:13:50,688
Right. I do feel comfortable.

1727
01:13:51,728 --> 01:13:53,598
I feel so comfortable at the thought of hanging out with you.

1728
01:13:53,598 --> 01:13:55,298
But don't feel to comfortable.

1729
01:13:55,398 --> 01:13:56,468
Okay.

1730
01:13:57,098 --> 01:13:59,638
Okay. I'll feel reasonably comfortable.

1731
01:14:01,008 --> 01:14:02,238
No. You can feel comfortable.

1732
01:14:02,238 --> 01:14:04,108
I like it that way.

1733
01:14:05,378 --> 01:14:09,548
(Ryun Gi carefully knocks at Ro Bin's heart.)

1734
01:14:09,948 --> 01:14:11,318
He's expressing himself so much.

1735
01:14:11,478 --> 01:14:13,018
This is one or the other.

1736
01:14:13,018 --> 01:14:14,748
They will end up liking each other...

1737
01:14:14,748 --> 01:14:17,388
- or become really close friends.
- Right.

1738
01:14:17,388 --> 01:14:18,518
- Right.
- It seems like Ro Bin...

1739
01:14:18,518 --> 01:14:19,518
is thinking of him as a friend.

1740
01:14:19,518 --> 01:14:20,688
Oh, no.

1741
01:14:20,688 --> 01:14:22,988
I think it takes quite a bit of time...

1742
01:14:22,988 --> 01:14:24,758
- to know their own heart.
- Right.

1743
01:14:25,028 --> 01:14:26,258
We don't know what to expect...

1744
01:14:26,258 --> 01:14:27,898
- Anything can happen.
- after the date.

1745
01:14:32,998 --> 01:14:35,138
- Shall we go out for a walk?
- Sure.

1746
01:14:35,968 --> 01:14:37,908
Put on something warm.

1747
01:14:38,178 --> 01:14:39,308
Where should we go?

1748
01:14:40,838 --> 01:14:42,008
- Outside?
- Okay.

1749
01:14:42,008 --> 01:14:43,048
The first floor.

1750
01:14:45,848 --> 01:14:46,948
Nice.

1751
01:14:47,348 --> 01:14:48,448
Where are you two going?

1752
01:14:48,788 --> 01:14:50,388
Why has Seon Ho changed so much?

1753
01:14:50,448 --> 01:14:51,758
Will he make things happen?

1754
01:14:52,258 --> 01:14:53,318
He must get things settled now.

1755
01:14:53,318 --> 01:14:54,328
Right.

1756
01:14:54,328 --> 01:14:56,128
Our Seon Ho has changed!

1757
01:14:56,888 --> 01:14:58,198
Has he really changed?

1758
01:15:00,598 --> 01:15:01,628
Gosh, it looks nice.

1759
01:15:01,628 --> 01:15:02,868
(Seon Ho asked to talk first for the first time.)

1760
01:15:02,868 --> 01:15:04,998
Right. It does look nice.

1761
01:15:14,208 --> 01:15:16,508
It's my first time... No. I came here earlier.

1762
01:15:16,508 --> 01:15:18,318
(The two sit facing each other in the quiet garden.)

1763
01:15:18,318 --> 01:15:19,318
Gosh.

1764
01:15:19,418 --> 01:15:20,418
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

1765
01:15:20,778 --> 01:15:22,988
- Did you have fun today?
- Today?

1766
01:15:23,288 --> 01:15:26,018
It's a simple question.

1767
01:15:26,118 --> 01:15:27,458
- Today?
- Yes.

1768
01:15:28,228 --> 01:15:30,658
Not as much as yesterday's date.

1769
01:15:33,598 --> 01:15:34,598
Did you have fun?

1770
01:15:34,598 --> 01:15:35,628
- Today?
- Yes.

1771
01:15:35,628 --> 01:15:38,468
Well, I didn't enjoy it as much.

1772
01:15:40,638 --> 01:15:43,768
But I tried to make the most of it.

1773
01:15:45,608 --> 01:15:46,678
Actually,

1774
01:15:47,648 --> 01:15:50,408
did you think that I didn't spend my time on you?

1775
01:15:51,148 --> 01:15:52,448
- Yesterday?
- Yes.

1776
01:15:55,818 --> 01:15:59,558
I knew that you...

1777
01:16:01,588 --> 01:16:02,628
spent your time on me yesterday.

1778
01:16:03,028 --> 01:16:04,058
- Yesterday?
- Yes.

1779
01:16:04,058 --> 01:16:05,128
How did you know?

1780
01:16:05,658 --> 01:16:08,398
Wouldn't you have spent your time on me?

1781
01:16:09,228 --> 01:16:10,898
But I didn't tell you that I spent my time on you.

1782
01:16:11,698 --> 01:16:14,168
I saw that you didn't go out for a date.

1783
01:16:14,938 --> 01:16:18,138
I thought that you had spent your time on me,

1784
01:16:18,238 --> 01:16:19,938
but things didn't work out.

1785
01:16:20,838 --> 01:16:22,578
- Am I right?
- Yes. You're right.

1786
01:16:25,118 --> 01:16:26,148
I see.

1787
01:16:29,118 --> 01:16:32,218
Did you want to spend time with me today?

1788
01:16:32,418 --> 01:16:33,488
- Today?
- Yes.

1789
01:16:35,428 --> 01:16:36,458
I hoped to...

1790
01:16:37,428 --> 01:16:39,058
if it were to be possible.

1791
01:16:40,698 --> 01:16:43,698
I enjoyed the time we spent during the last two dates.

1792
01:16:45,868 --> 01:16:47,538
I admit that I was curious about you.

1793
01:16:47,938 --> 01:16:50,308
I wanted to know if my heart had an interest...

1794
01:16:50,308 --> 01:16:51,608
or something beyond an interest.

1795
01:16:51,808 --> 01:16:54,038
I wasn't hiding my feelings.

1796
01:16:54,038 --> 01:16:56,108
I just wasn't sure...

1797
01:16:57,848 --> 01:16:58,878
about my feelings.

1798
01:16:59,578 --> 01:17:00,818
But now,

1799
01:17:01,188 --> 01:17:04,888
I feel like I should follow my heart.

1800
01:17:05,788 --> 01:17:08,958
I should move the way my heart moves.

1801
01:17:09,658 --> 01:17:11,358
These were the thoughts I had.

1802
01:17:12,198 --> 01:17:14,928
We've spent almost half of our time here.

1803
01:17:15,528 --> 01:17:16,628
Tomorrow...

1804
01:17:16,628 --> 01:17:18,198
- it will be over half of our time.
- It's our fifth day.

1805
01:17:20,938 --> 01:17:23,908
Do you think things will become clear...

1806
01:17:24,338 --> 01:17:27,108
after tomorrow's date?

1807
01:17:28,778 --> 01:17:32,618
Yes. I feel like things will become clear after tomorrow.

1808
01:17:34,618 --> 01:17:35,788
What about you, Ye Ji?

1809
01:17:35,788 --> 01:17:38,618
Are things clear for you?

1810
01:17:39,418 --> 01:17:42,588
Actually,

1811
01:17:42,588 --> 01:17:46,198
up until yesterday, you were the only one...

1812
01:17:46,198 --> 01:17:47,968
- I talked to.
- Right.

1813
01:17:48,468 --> 01:17:51,138
I went on a date...

1814
01:17:52,168 --> 01:17:54,808
with someone else today,

1815
01:17:58,038 --> 01:18:00,138
but I kept getting reminded about yesterday.

1816
01:18:01,548 --> 01:18:04,148
(Smirking)

1817
01:18:04,148 --> 01:18:05,348
So...

1818
01:18:07,218 --> 01:18:09,188
- That's so cute!
- My gosh.

1819
01:18:09,418 --> 01:18:10,688
(Bursting out in laughter)

1820
01:18:10,688 --> 01:18:12,188
It feels like we're peeking on them.

1821
01:18:12,188 --> 01:18:13,588
- Right.
- Right?

1822
01:18:13,588 --> 01:18:15,588
I don't know why I'm holding my breath.

1823
01:18:15,688 --> 01:18:16,958
Isn't it so nice to talk like this?

1824
01:18:16,958 --> 01:18:18,528
Right. It's great.

1825
01:18:18,728 --> 01:18:22,768
- I won't feel anxious anymore.
- Right.

1826
01:18:24,028 --> 01:18:25,938
A date will surely happen, right?

